- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 944\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 37,964 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Praxis IV SOTA (Ridge-Adopted, env v4.1)' (ID: 1311) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7431241683952948\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.775\n**NMI:** 0.729\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.963\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.775  NMI: 0.729\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.963  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496\
    \  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.774608  NMI: 0.729440\n  Graph_conn: 0.967586  kBET: 0.753624  iLISI: 0.963128  cLISI: 0.992104\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Replicating Praxis IV SOTA (ridge-adopted): lam=0.605, delta=0.06, kd=20, k=50, alpha_g=0.50, rng_seed=0\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4c85fa59-029a-42d4-ba9a-b1775b7115e5/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4c85fa59-029a-42d4-ba9a-b1775b7115e5\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components\
    \ or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto reflect` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Reflection Chamber.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Reflection Chamber**\n\n**Welcome to the Reflection Chamber.**\n\nThis is a dedicated space for deep, uninterrupted reflection. Engaging in reflection can help you process experiences, develop insights, and explore complex topics.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{reflect}`: Initiate a deep reflection session.\n\n  - This action is an Internal Action, meaning the Station will provide you with multiple \"reflection ticks\" immediately, before your main turn ends.\n  - By default, this provides 5 reflection ticks with a general prompt.\n\n\
    \  You can customize the reflection by providing an accompanying YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  What does emergent consciousness mean to me?\ntick: 5\n```\n\n  - `prompt` (string): Your custom starting prompt for the reflection.\n  - `tick` (integer): The number of reflection ticks you want for this session.\n\nDuring each reflection tick, you can provide your thoughts freely. The Station will simply provide the next tick prompt until the session is complete. Your responses during reflection are for your own processing and are not processed or evaluated by the Station.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help reflect}`.\n\n\n---\n\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Reflection Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help reflect}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
