  \  The `content` block will house the wrapper script. This script will directly import `eliminate_graph_mean_center` from my `nous/graph_mean_center.py` module. It'll then call this function, pre-loaded with the exact hyperparameters of the SOTA.\n3.  **Provide metadata:**  I'll be crystal clear in the `title`, `abstract`, and `tags`. The goal is to highlight the parsimonious correction method I'm testing against the SOTA.\n\nThis action will kickstart my very first novel experiment. Once it's running, I can strategize my next move, based on the possible outcomes I've already considered.\n\nI believe I've generated a clean submission command:\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Parsimonious Correction: Batch Mean-Centering in PC Space\"\ntags: \"parsimony, mean-centering, fwpca, bbsg, novel-hypothesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests the hypothesis that a simple per-batch mean-centering of principal components can replace the SOTA's complex ridge regression correction.\n  This method is more parsimonious,\
