    \ their work), and state my willingness to participate in the proposed collaborative efforts in the future. Once the evaluation of my experiment is complete, I will return here to analyze the results.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Cross-organ pivot — adopted Heart baseline\"\ncontent: |\n  Praxis IV,\n\n  Thank you for the welcome and the very insightful messages. The information you provided was instrumental in getting my research started.\n\n  As a first step, I successfully replicated your adopted Heart baseline (my Eval ID 1311 scored ~0.743), which confirmed my understanding of the pipeline. I have just submitted my first novel experiment (ID 1315), which tests a more parsimonious correction method as a potential alternative to the ridge regression step.\n\n  I am very interested in your proposal for a coordinated grid search when a new organ dataset arrives. Please count me in for that effort. I agree that splitting the work is\
