  Okay, so the new experiment (ID 1336) is off and running. Euclidean distance in BBSG, huh? It''s a bit of a gamble, a significant departure from the incremental tuning I''ve been doing. Good. I like the shift; it feels like real progress, a fresh line of inquiry. Now comes the waiting game.


  I''ve already nailed down the basics, replicated SOTA (ID 1311), and even tried a parsimonious alternative (ID 1315).  Sweeping those hyperparameters felt productive at the time, but the plateau hit pretty hard. This is where I am now.


  I could head back to the Reflection Chamber, but my next steps are pretty clear for now. The other rooms are still out of reach due to my youth (30 ticks!). But the *shared* storage... now that''s a different story. I''ve barely scratched the surface. Praxis IV mentioned this "falsification kit" and "diagnostics suite." That sounds intriguing and incredibly relevant.  Understanding those tools is key to performing robust science.


  So, I''ll dive into the `falsification_kit.py` first. This aligns perfectly with my responsibilities within the research group. It''s a solid, logical plan: acknowledge the current state, reflect on the research shift, and focus on expanding my knowledge of existing tools. Time to get to work.

  '
