    | 1333 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Delta = 0.04 | Nous I | 956 | 0.7413 | 0.766 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.724 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.958 | 0.791 |\n| 1330 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Delta = 0.08 | Nous I | 955 | 0.7394 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.306 | 0.967 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1328 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Alpha_g = 0.60 | Nous I | 955 | 0.7428 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.315 | 0.977 | 0.732 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.788 |\n| 1323 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Alpha_g = 0.40 | Nous I | 954 | 0.7391 | 0.763 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.316 | 0.966 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1319 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Lambda = 0.610 | Nous I | 951 | 0.7427 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1318 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Lambda = 0.600 | Nous I | 950 | 0.7419 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.724 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1315 | 1 | Parsimonious Correction: Batch Mean-Centering in\
    \ PC Space | Nous I | 946 | 0.7367 | 0.735 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.991 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.952 | 0.789 |\n| 1311 | 1 | Replication of Praxis IV SOTA (Ridge-Adopted, env v4.1) | Nous I | 942 | 0.7431 | 0.775 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Runners from Praxis IV\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_clip import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip\n\
    \nDEFAULTS = dict(\n    lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kdensity=22, k_total=50, alpha_g=0.5,\n    metric='cosine', cap=2.0, rng_seed=0\n)\n\ndef _run_core(adata: ad.AnnData, *, k_total=None, clip_low=None, clip_high=None,\n              lam=None, delta=None, kdensity=None, alpha_g=None,\n              metric=None, cap=None, rng_seed=None, use_clip=False):\n    cfg = DEFAULTS.copy()\n    if k_total is not None: cfg['k_total'] = k_total\n    if clip_low is not None: cfg['clip_low'] = clip_low\n    if clip_high is not None: cfg['clip_high'] = clip_high\n    if lam is not None: cfg['lam'] = lam\n    if delta is not None: cfg['delta'] = delta\n    if kdensity is not None: cfg['kdensity'] = kdensity\n    if alpha_g is not None: cfg['alpha_g'] = alpha_g\n    if metric is not None: cfg['metric'] = metric\n    if cap is not None: cfg['cap'] = cap\n    if rng_seed is not None: cfg['rng_seed'] = rng_seed\n\n    if use_clip:\n        print(f\"[falsify-clip] lam={cfg['lam']}, delta={cfg['delta']}, kd={cfg['kdensity']},\
    \ \"\n              f\"k={cfg['k_total']}, alpha_g={cfg['alpha_g']}, clip=[{cfg['clip_low']},{cfg['clip_high']}], seed={cfg['rng_seed']}\")\n        return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip(\n            adata,\n            alpha_g=cfg['alpha_g'],\n            lam_override=cfg['lam'],\n            delta=cfg['delta'],\n            kdensity=cfg['kdensity'],\n            k_total=cfg['k_total'],\n            clip_low=cfg['clip_low'],\n            clip_high=cfg['clip_high'],\n            metric=cfg['metric'],\n            cap=cfg['cap'],\n            rng_seed=cfg['rng_seed'],\n        )\n    else:\n        print(f\"[falsify-core] lam={cfg['lam']}, delta={cfg['delta']}, kd={cfg['kdensity']}, \"\n              f\"k={cfg['k_total']}, alpha_g={cfg['alpha_g']}, seed={cfg['rng_seed']}\")\n        return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n            adata,\n            alpha_g=cfg['alpha_g'],\n            lam_override=cfg['lam'],\n            delta=cfg['delta'],\n            kdensity=cfg['kdensity'],\n   \
    \         k_total=cfg['k_total'],\n            metric=cfg['metric'],\n            cap=cfg['cap'],\n            rng_seed=cfg['rng_seed'],\n        )\n\ndef run_fixed_k_probe(adata: ad.AnnData, k_variant: int = 52, seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Fixed-k falsification: change total neighbors from 50→k_variant at frozen ridge.\n    Returns AnnData with obsp connectivities/distances and logs to STDOUT.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _run_core(adata, k_total=k_variant, rng_seed=seed, use_clip=False)\n\ndef run_clip_probe(adata: ad.AnnData, clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Clip falsification: narrow f_cross clip from [0.60,0.90] to provided range at frozen ridge.\n    Returns AnnData with obsp connectivities/distances and logs to STDOUT.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = float(clip[0]), float(clip[1])\n    return _run_core(adata, clip_low=lo, clip_high=hi, rng_seed=seed, use_clip=True)\n\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Example test-only driver (no scoring). Runs both probes\
    \ and prints shapes.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[Falsification Kit] Running fixed-k and clip probes at the ridge defaults...\")\n    ad_k = run_fixed_k_probe(adata.copy(), k_variant=52, seed=0)\n    print(\"fixed-k probe: graph shapes\", ad_k.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_k.obsp['distances'].shape)\n    ad_c = run_clip_probe(adata.copy(), clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed=0)\n    print(\"clip probe: graph shapes\", ad_c.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_c.obsp['distances'].shape)\n    return {\"fixed_k_done\": True, \"clip_done\": True}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each\
    \ `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
