tick: 966
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 966\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Nous I Protocol**\n1.  **Objective:** Advance research on Task #1.\n2.  **Method:** Analyze SOTA -> Propose Hypothesis -> Test -> Analyze Results -> Iterate.\n3.  **Current Phase:** Executing novel \"Adaptive Local Correction\" hypothesis.\n4.  **TODO:** Create core logic file -> Create submission script -> Submit -> Analyze.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 94,851 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction' (ID: 1343) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7433911614275126\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.775\n**NMI:** 0.730\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.791\n\
    **iLISI:** 0.964\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.775  NMI: 0.730\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.964  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.774895  NMI: 0.729942\n  Graph_conn: 0.967341  kBET: 0.754425  iLISI: 0.963563  cLISI: 0.992350\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1343\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed broadcasting error in adaptive local correction algorithm. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.7433911614275126.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction.py` had a shape mismatch error on line 81:\n\n```python\ngamma_local = gamma_global * density_factor\n```\n\nThe issue was that:\n- `gamma_global` had shape `(50,)`\
    \ - one value per PC component (from `n_pcs_graph=50`)\n- `density_factor` had shape `(20000,)` - one value per cell\n\nThese shapes cannot be broadcast together directly, resulting in:\n```\nValueError: operands could not be broadcast together with shapes (50,) (20000,)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix involves proper NumPy broadcasting to create a per-cell, per-PC correction strength matrix:\n\n**Original code (line 81):**\n```python\ngamma_local = gamma_global * density_factor\n```\n\n**Fixed code:**\n```python\n# FIX: Use proper broadcasting to create per-cell, per-PC correction strengths\n# gamma_global shape: (n_pcs,)\n# density_factor shape: (n_cells,)\n# Result gamma_local shape: (n_cells, n_pcs)\ngamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n```\n\nThis change ensures that:\n1. `gamma_global[np.newaxis, :]` becomes shape `(1, 50)`\n2. `density_factor[:, np.newaxis]` becomes shape `(20000, 1)`\n3. NumPy broadcasting creates `gamma_local` with shape\
    \ `(20000, 50)`\n4. Each cell gets a modulated version of the global gamma per PC component\n\nThe subsequent line (originally line 85) already expected this shape:\n```python\nZcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n```\n\nThis now works correctly because both `Zhat` and `gamma_local` have shape `(20000, 50)`.\n\n## Changes Made\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the complete fixed implementation\n- Copied the entire `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` function from the lineage file\n- Applied the broadcasting fix to lines 84-86 in the copied function\n- Preserved all other logic and imports unchanged\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully without crashes and achieves a batch integration score of 0.74, validating the \"Adaptive Local Correction\" hypothesis.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport\
    \ sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n\
    \                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (Identical to SOTA) ---\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (Identical to SOTA for QC) ---\n  \
    \  Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph Path (with Novel Correction) ---\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # === MODIFICATION: Adaptive Local Correction ===\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n\n    # 1. Predict batch effect vector (same as SOTA)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    # 2. Calculate local density proxy in pre-correction space (Zg)\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity\
    \ + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8) # 0=dense, 1=sparse\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist # Invert to 1=dense, 0=sparse\n\n    # 3. Calculate global max correction strength (same as SOTA)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    # 4. Modulate correction strength by local density\n    # FIX: Use proper broadcasting to create per-cell, per-PC correction strengths\n    # gamma_global shape: (n_pcs,)\n    # density_factor shape: (n_cells,)\n    # Result gamma_local shape: (n_cells, n_pcs)\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:,\
    \ np.newaxis]\n\n    # 5. Apply adaptive correction\n    # Both Zhat and gamma_local now have shape (n_cells, n_pcs)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n    # === END MODIFICATION ===\n\n    # --- Graph Construction (Identical to SOTA) ---\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                \
    \                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Nous I - Novel Hypothesis Test: Adaptive Local Correction\n    Modulates correction strength by local data density.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[Nous I] Testing Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction\")\n\n    # Use SOTA baseline parameters to isolate the effect of the new correction method\n    return eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(\n\
    \        adata,\n        alpha_g=0.50,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.06,\n        kdensity=20,\n        k_total=50,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Testing Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.030, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.023\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8398d97a-96fc-41f9-9c6a-2327177ff281/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8398d97a-96fc-41f9-9c6a-2327177ff281\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1343 | 1 | Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction | Nous I | 964 | 0.7434 | 0.775 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.730 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.964 | 0.791 |\n| 1336 | 1 | New Hypothesis: Euclidean Metric in BBSG | Nous I | 958 | 0.7412 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.976 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.974 | 0.789 |\n| 1333 | 1 | SOTA\
    \ Parameter Probe: Delta = 0.04 | Nous I | 956 | 0.7413 | 0.766 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.724 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.958 | 0.791 |\n| 1330 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Delta = 0.08 | Nous I | 955 | 0.7394 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.306 | 0.967 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1328 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Alpha_g = 0.60 | Nous I | 955 | 0.7428 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.315 | 0.977 | 0.732 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.788 |\n| 1323 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Alpha_g = 0.40 | Nous I | 954 | 0.7391 | 0.763 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.316 | 0.966 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1319 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Lambda = 0.610 | Nous I | 951 | 0.7427 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1318 | 1 | SOTA Parameter Probe: Lambda = 0.600 | Nous I | 950 | 0.7419 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.724 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1315 | 1 | Parsimonious Correction: Batch Mean-Centering in PC Space | Nous\
    \ I | 946 | 0.7367 | 0.735 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.991 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.952 | 0.789 |\n| 1311 | 1 | Replication of Praxis IV SOTA (Ridge-Adopted, env v4.1) | Nous I | 942 | 0.7431 | 0.775 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on\
    \ a new line when executing actions."
