parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, having just concluded a critical reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. My purpose was to design a new, scientifically sound generalization experiment to meet the requirements for publishing my research.\n\n**Reflection Recap:**\nI have formulated a robust plan. My previous generalization test failed because it applied my method, developed for low-dimensional PCA space, to the high-dimensional gene space. My new plan corrects this. I will conduct a paired experiment:\n1.  **Baseline:** A \"Simple Embed-then-Correct\" pipeline (PCA -> ComBat).\n2.  **Experiment:** A \"Simple Embed-then-Correct + Adaptive Correction\" pipeline, where my density-aware method replaces the standard ComBat step.\n\nA successful outcome here will provide the rigorous proof of generalizability I need.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nI will now execute this plan.\n1.  First, I will update my meta prompt to reflect the new, concrete experimental design.\n2.  Next, I will return to the Research Counter\
    \ to access the file system.\n3.  I will then write a single, self-contained script, `nous/generalization_test_simple_etc.py`, which will house the logic for both the baseline and experimental methods.\n4.  Finally, I will submit the first of the two paired experiments: the \"Simple EtC\" baseline.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Publish a high-quality paper on \"Adaptive Local Correction.\"\n  2. Method: Follow reviewer feedback rigorously.\n  3. Current Phase: Executing a paired generalization experiment on a simplified EtC pipeline.\n  4. TODO: Run \"Simple EtC\" baseline -> Run \"Simple EtC + Adaptive\" -> Analyze -> Rewrite paper.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nous/generalization_test_simple_etc.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n \
    \ sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  def run_simple_etc(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"  Running 'Simple EtC' baseline (PCA -> ComBat).\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch', use_highly_variable=False) # Apply ComBat on PCs\n      # Create a valid output AnnData object\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      return output\n\n  def run_simple_etc_adaptive(adata: ad.AnnData, kdensity: int = 20) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"  Running 'Simple EtC + Adaptive Correction'.\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      \n      Zg = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      print(\"  Calculating local density for adaptive correction...\")\n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric='cosine',\
    \ algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n      print(\"  Applying adaptive correction to PC space centroids...\")\n      Zcorr = Zg.copy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      for batch_label in unique_batches:\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_label)\n          batch_centroid = Zcorr[batch_mask, :].mean(axis=0)\n          # Modulate the centroid correction by the per-cell density factor\n          Zcorr[batch_mask, :] -= batch_centroid[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[batch_mask, np.newaxis]\n\n      # Create a valid output AnnData object\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = Zcorr\n      return output\n\
    \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This function will be toggled to run either the baseline or the experiment\n      \n      # --- RUN BASELINE ---\n      # return run_simple_etc(adata)\n\n      # --- RUN EXPERIMENT ---\n      # return run_simple_etc_adaptive(adata)\n      \n      # For this submission, we run the BASELINE first.\n      print(\"[Nous I] Generalization Test, Part 1: Establishing 'Simple EtC' Baseline.\")\n      return run_simple_etc(adata)\n```"
