parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 990\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Publish a high-quality paper on \"Adaptive Local Correction.\"\n2. Method: Follow reviewer feedback rigorously.\n3. Current Phase: Executing a paired generalization experiment on a simplified EtC pipeline.\n4. TODO: Run \"Simple EtC\" baseline -> Run \"Simple EtC + Adaptive\" -> Analyze -> Rewrite paper.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,029 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 61 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Generalization Test (1/2): Simple EtC Baseline' (ID: 1377) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.45476788895678066\n\
    **ASW_batch:** 0.516\n**ASW_label:** 0.208\n**ARI:** 0.415\n**NMI:** 0.649\n**Graph_conn:** 0.890\n**kBET:** 0.529\n**iLISI:** 0.003\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.348\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.516  ASW_label: 0.208  ARI: 0.415  NMI: 0.649\n  Graph_conn: 0.890  kBET: 0.529  iLISI: 0.003  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.348\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.765899  ASW_label: 0.531615  ARI: 0.415219  NMI: 0.648708\n  Graph_conn: 0.891715  kBET: 0.508447  iLISI: 0.002880  cLISI: 0.997306\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.305354\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1377\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on the first attempt. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with a `TypeError` on line 15 of the submission:\n```\nTypeError: combat() got an unexpected keyword argument 'use_highly_variable'\n```\n\
    \nThe issue was in this line:\n```python\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch', use_highly_variable=False)\n```\n\nThe `sc.pp.combat()` function from Scanpy does not accept a `use_highly_variable` parameter. This parameter was likely copied from another Scanpy function (like `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes()`) where it would be valid, but it's not a valid parameter for the ComBat batch correction function.\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the invalid `use_highly_variable=False` parameter from the `sc.pp.combat()` call.\n\n**Original line (submission_v1):**\n```python\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch', use_highly_variable=False)  # Apply ComBat on PCs\n```\n\n**Fixed line (submission_v2):**\n```python\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')  # Apply ComBat on PCs - removed use_highly_variable parameter\n```\n\n## Verification\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the fix\n- Ran `monitor_evaluation.py 2` to verify the fix\n- Exit code 0 (SUCCESS) - Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- The\
    \ batch integration algorithm is now executing correctly\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Task**: Batch effect correction using PCA and ComBat method\n- **Error Type**: Invalid function parameter (API mismatch)\n- **Fix Complexity**: Simple - removed one invalid parameter\n- **Testing**: Verified the code runs successfully for the full evaluation timeout period\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\ndef run_simple_etc(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"  Running 'Simple EtC' baseline (PCA -> ComBat).\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata,\
