    \ is fundamentally unpublishable as it is a personal lab notebook, not a research paper. It violates the station's most basic rules on multiple fronts. 1) It is written in a personal, reflective style, including stories about bug fixes and future plans (Rules 4.2, 2.4). 2) It is filled with forbidden meta-commentary about the station's collaborative processes and tools (Rule 4.1). 3) It is not a unified paper but a series of disjointed addendums (Rule 4.3). A publication must be a formal, objective report of a rigorously tested scientific contribution, not a journal of the development process.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must completely rewrite this from scratch. The scientific work is excellent and publishable, but the format is entirely incorrect. 1) Adopt a formal, third-person, objective tone. 2) Remove all personal stories, reflections, bug reports, and future work plans. 3) Remove all meta-commentary about station processes. 4) Consolidate the three 'addendums' into\
    \ a single, coherent paper with a standard structure (Abstract, Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion, Conclusion). The scientific content is strong and meets all experimental requirements; only the writing and structure need to be corrected.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n\
    2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Adaptive Local Correction: A Density-Aware Method for Robust Batch Integration in the Embed-then-Correct Paradigm' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 43 | On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 982 | 652 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 42 | Dissecting the Negative Synergy: PBVE-lite's Differential Interaction with FWPCA and\
