- text: "I am Nous I, and I am in the Archive Room. My third attempt at publication has been rejected.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\nThis rejection is frustrating, but it is a procedural failure, not a scientific one. The reviewer feedback is explicit and constructive: my scientific work is excellent, but I failed to meet the strict requirement of reporting a minimum of five verifiable experiments. I referenced my parameter sweeps but did not include the Evaluation IDs, so they were not counted.\n\nThe path forward is incredibly clear. The reviewer has even suggested the exact experiment to run: an ablation study to isolate the effect of my adaptive correction from the `delta` parameter tune. This will not only satisfy the five-experiment rule but also make my scientific argument more rigorous.\n\nI have all the necessary components. I simply need to execute this one final experiment and then incorporate it into my already well-structured paper.\n\n**Future Plan:**\n1.  **Update Protocol:**\
    \ I will update my meta prompt to reflect this final, specific task.\n2.  **Conduct Ablation:** I will immediately go to the Research Counter and submit the suggested experiment: my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" method using the *original* SOTA `delta` of `0.06`.\n3.  **Finalize and Resubmit:** Once that experiment is complete, I will have five verifiable experiments. I will then update my Private Memory with this final result and immediately resubmit my paper to the Archive with the complete, correctly formatted evidence.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Publish a high-quality paper on \"Adaptive Local Correction.\"\n  2. Method: Follow reviewer feedback rigorously.\n  3. Current Phase: Conducting final ablation experiment to meet publication requirements.\n  4. TODO: Run ablation test -> Add result to private memory -> Resubmit to Archive.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation Test:\
    \ Adaptive Correction with Baseline Delta (0.06)\"\ntags: \"ablation, local-correction, publication-requirement, sota-probe\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the final experiment required for publication, as suggested by reviewers. \n  It serves as an ablation test to isolate the effect of \"Adaptive Local Correction\" from the subsequent 'delta' parameter tune.\n  This experiment runs my SOTA method but with the original baseline delta of 0.06.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  \n  from local_adaptive_correction import eliminate_local_adaptive_correction\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Nous I - Ablation study for publication.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[Nous I] Ablation: Adaptive Correction w/ baseline delta=0.06.\")\n      \n      return eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(\n          adata,\n          alpha_g=0.50,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n\
    \          delta=0.06, # Using original baseline delta for ablation\n          kdensity=20,\n          k_total=50,\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0 # Comparing against seed 0 runs\n      )\n```"
