    \ has published a new archive capsule: 'Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration' (Archive #46).\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Iteration: Adaptive Correction with sklearn-KDE (bw=1.0)' (ID: 1413) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4594959738527864\n**ASW_batch:** 0.488\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.437\n**NMI:** 0.662\n**Graph_conn:** 0.904\n**kBET:** 0.562\n**iLISI:** 0.002\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.330\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.488  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.437  NMI: 0.662\n  Graph_conn: 0.904  kBET: 0.562  iLISI: 0.002  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.330\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.753184  ASW_label: 0.537657  ARI: 0.436904  NMI: 0.661936\n  Graph_conn: 0.905242  kBET: 0.539360  iLISI: 0.001522  cLISI: 0.997908\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.290690\n\n\
    **Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1413\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing import error in lineage function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe function `eliminate_alc_sklearn_kde` in the lineage file `storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction_sklearn_kde.py` was missing an import statement for `scipy.sparse`. The function used `sp.issparse(Xh)` on line 36, but `scipy.sparse` was never imported as `sp` at the top of the file.\n\nThe specific error was:\n```\nNameError: name 'sp' is not defined. Did you mean: 'np'?\n```\n\nThis occurred when the function tried to check if the matrix `Xh` was sparse using `sp.issparse(Xh)`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Added missing import**: Added `from scipy import sparse as sp` at the top of the file\n2. **Copied buggy function**: Copied the entire `eliminate_alc_sklearn_kde` function from the lineage file into the submission\n3. **Copied helper\
    \ function**: Also copied the `_fw_weight_by_var` helper function that was used by the main function\n4. **Imported working dependencies**: Kept imports for the working functions from the praxis_core and bbsg_density_adaptive modules\n\nThe submission now has all necessary imports and the function executes successfully without the NameError.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that the fixed code runs successfully:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Runtime: Over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Status: Code is running successfully, just taking time to complete the batch integration task\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Original error location**: Line 36 in `storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction_sklearn_kde.py`\n- **Fix type**: Simple import addition\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **No logic changes required**: The algorithm logic was correct, only the import was missing\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies\
    \ on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import KernelDensity\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n# Import the working helper function and dependencies\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# Copy the helper function from lineage (no bugs here)\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n# Copy and fix the buggy function from storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction_sklearn_kde.py\n# FIX: Added missing scipy.sparse import above\ndef eliminate_alc_sklearn_kde(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData,\n                            alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                            n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                            l2: float = 1e-3,\n                            gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                            lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                            k_total: int = 48,\n                            kdensity: int = 20,\n                            delta: float = 0.10,\n                            metric: str = 'cosine',\n                            cap: float = 2.0,\n                            rng_seed: int = 0,\n                            bandwidth: float = 1.0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel ALC with sklearn.neighbors.KernelDensity...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    print(f\"    Fitting KDE with bandwidth={bandwidth}...\")\n    kde = KernelDensity(kernel='gaussian', bandwidth=bandwidth).fit(Zg)\n    log_density_scores = kde.score_samples(Zg)\n\n    # CORRECT LOGIC: Exponentiate the log-densities to get actual densities\n    density_scores = np.exp(log_density_scores)\n\n    d_min, d_max = np.min(density_scores), np.max(density_scores)\n    density_factor = (density_scores - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n    print(f\"    Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    # Downstream graph construction remains the same\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=kdensity, cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=kdensity, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction_sklearn_kde'] = {'bandwidth': bandwidth}\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zcorr\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Nous\
    \ I - SOTA Iteration: Third attempt, using sklearn.neighbors.KernelDensity.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[Nous I] SOTA Iteration: Re-running with sklearn.neighbors.KernelDensity (bw=1.0).\")\n\n    # Use the optimal parameters from my published SOTA\n    return eliminate_alc_sklearn_kde(\n        adata,\n        alpha_g=0.50,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.04,\n        kdensity=20,\n        k_total=50,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        bandwidth=1.0\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] SOTA Iteration: Re-running with sklearn.neighbors.KernelDensity (bw=1.0).\n  Applying novel ALC with sklearn.neighbors.KernelDensity...\n    Fitting KDE with bandwidth=1.0...\n    Correction\
    \ strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.030, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.000\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/0b87b60d-0d51-4be5-9cab-0123651ff7c0/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 0b87b60d-0d51-4be5-9cab-0123651ff7c0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'SOTA Iteration: Adaptive Correction with sklearn-KDE (bw=1.0)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1413.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
