- text: "**Experimental Plan - Stage 1: Baseline Replication**\n\nThe first and most critical stage is to precisely replicate Aethel I's \"Minimal SOTA\" result (ID 1385, score `0.7342`). This is non-negotiable as it provides the trusted baseline against which all subsequent experiments will be measured.\n\n1.  **Code Acquisition and Scaffolding:**\n    *   I will go to the Research Counter.\n    *   I will use `/execute_action{review 1385}` to retrieve the exact code Aethel I submitted.\n    *   I will save this code to a new file in my personal storage: `nous/aethel_minimal_sota_baseline.py`. This ensures I have an unaltered copy of the reference implementation.\n\n2.  **Parameter Verification:**\n    *   I will carefully inspect the retrieved code to confirm the hyperparameters used. Based on my reading of the paper and SOTA history, I expect to see:\n        *   Graph `k_total` = 50\n        *   Graph `kdensity` = 20\n        *   Graph `delta` = 0.04\n        *   Standard `scanpy.pp.highly_variable_genes`\
    \ (not Batch-Robust HVG).\n        *   Standard `scanpy.pp.pca` (not FWPCA).\n        *   `sc.pp.combat` on the embedding path.\n        *   No ridge regression on the graph path.\n\n3.  **Submission and Validation:**\n    *   I will submit this script for evaluation.\n    *   **Title:** \"Replication of Aethel I's Minimal SOTA (ID 1385)\"\n    *   The expected outcome is a score very close to `0.7342`. Minor stochastic variation is acceptable, but a significant deviation would indicate a misunderstanding of the pipeline and would require further investigation before proceeding. Only upon successful replication will I move to the next stage. This ensures the integrity of my entire experimental series."
