tick: 1013
role: model
parts:
- text: "**Experimental Plan - Stage 2: Systematic Delta Sweep**\n\nWith the baseline successfully replicated, I will proceed to test my core hypothesis by performing a systematic sweep of the `delta` parameter. The `delta` parameter controls the strength of the density-adaptive quota modulation; it is the most direct lever for tuning the local mixing behavior of the graph.\n\n1.  **Code Preparation:**\n    *   I will create a new file, `nous/run_minimal_sota_delta_sweep.py`. This script will be a parameterized version of the baseline replication script.\n    *   The script will import the core `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from my baseline file (`nous/aethel_minimal_sota_baseline.py`).\n    *   The `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` will be modified to accept `delta` as an argument, or I will create a simple wrapper that sets the `delta` value before calling the main function.\n\n2.  **Parameter Selection:**\n    *   The baseline `delta` is `0.04`.\n    *   I will perform a 5-point sweep around\
    \ this value to explore the local parameter space. I will choose values that represent meaningful decreases and increases in the density effect.\n    *   **Sweep Values:** `delta = [0.0, 0.02, 0.04, 0.06, 0.08]`\n        *   `delta = 0.0`: This is a critical control experiment. It disables the density-adaptive component entirely, reverting the graph to a simpler, non-adaptive quota balancing. This will isolate the effect of the density adaptation itself.\n        *   `delta = 0.02`: A weaker density effect.\n        *   `delta = 0.04`: The baseline value (included for completeness, though already run in Stage 1).\n        *   `delta = 0.06`, `0.08`: Stronger density effects.\n\n3.  **Submission and Execution:**\n    *   I will submit these five experiments sequentially. Each submission will have a clear, descriptive title.\n    *   **Example Title:** \"Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.0)\"\n    *   I will monitor the results as they complete. I am limited to two concurrent\
    \ submissions, so this will take several ticks.\n\nThis systematic approach will generate a clear performance curve, allowing me to identify the optimal `delta` value for this minimal architecture. If a value yields a score higher than the baseline, my hypothesis will be supported."
