- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1016\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Discover a new SOTA by optimizing Aethel I's \"Minimal SOTA\" pipeline.\n2. Method: Replicate baseline -> Systematically sweep key parameters (`delta`) -> Analyze -> Iterate.\n3. Current Phase: Executing Stage 1 - Baseline Replication.\n4. TODO: Replicate Aethel's Minimal SOTA (ID 1385) -> Begin Stage 2 (Delta Sweep).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 71,159 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 87 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Aethel I's Minimal SOTA (ID 1385)' (ID: 1422) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6232549041368627\n\
    **ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.596\n**NMI:** 0.686\n**Graph_conn:** 0.882\n**kBET:** 0.783\n**iLISI:** 0.036\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.363\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.596  NMI: 0.686\n  Graph_conn: 0.882  kBET: 0.783  iLISI: 0.036  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.363\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.595452  NMI: 0.686349\n  Graph_conn: 0.883727  kBET: 0.747298  iLISI: 0.036298  cLISI: 0.996279\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.318539\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Minimal SOTA\
    \ Pipeline] Simplified Dual-Path Integration.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/d782b5d7-1140-4bae-8193-9e1f941dfbd4/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: d782b5d7-1140-4bae-8193-9e1f941dfbd4\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.0, Control)' (ID: 1423) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6204467772293475\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.596\n**NMI:** 0.686\n**Graph_conn:** 0.882\n**kBET:** 0.785\n**iLISI:** 0.036\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.334\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.596  NMI: 0.686\n  Graph_conn: 0.882  kBET: 0.785  iLISI: 0.036  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.334\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.595452  NMI: 0.686349\n  Graph_conn: 0.883727  kBET: 0.748775  iLISI: 0.036298  cLISI: 0.996279\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.293283\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1423\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the function signature mismatch error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission created a wrapper function called `final_eliminate_batch_effect_fn` that called the imported `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` with `delta_override=0.0`. However, the evaluation system's `main.py` expects to find a function named `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` with the signature `eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData`.\n\nThe error was:\n```\nTypeError: eliminate_batch_effect_fn() missing 1 required positional argument: 'delta_override'\n```\n\nThis occurred because:\n1. The system called `eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata_input)` with only one argument\n2. The imported function from\
    \ `storage/nous/parameterized_minimal_sota.py` requires two arguments: `adata` and `delta_override`\n3. The wrapper function was named incorrectly (`final_eliminate_batch_effect_fn` instead of `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`)\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Imported helper functions only**: Kept the working helper functions from the lineage file (`normalize_log1p_inplace`, `pca_array`, `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`, `get_standard_hvgs`)\n\n2. **Redefined the main function**: Created `eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData` with the correct signature that the system expects\n\n3. **Hardcoded delta value**: Set `delta_override = 0.0` inside the function body, matching the agent's intent for a control experiment\n\n4. **Preserved all logic**: The function performs the exact same computation as the original lineage function, just with the delta parameter hardcoded\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the code\
    \ has been running successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, which indicates the fix is working correctly. The evaluation may take time to complete due to the computational intensity of the batch integration algorithm, but the code is executing properly.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Version created**: submission_v2.py\n- **Fix type**: Function signature correction + parameter hardcoding\n- **Functions imported from lineage**: All helper functions (working correctly)\n- **Functions redefined**: Only `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` (to fix signature mismatch)\n- **Delta value**: 0.0 (control experiment - no density adaptation)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\
    from typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# Import working helper functions from lineage\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nfrom parameterized_minimal_sota import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, build_density_adaptive_bbsg, get_standard_hvgs\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Control baseline: delta = 0.0 (no density adaptation)\n    \"\"\"\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    k_total = 50\n    kdensity = 20\n    rng_seed = 0\n    delta_override = 0.0  # Control: no density adaptation\n\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    hvg_names = get_standard_hvgs(adata, n_genes=2000)\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var_names.isin(hvg_names)\n    hv_mask = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xd = (adata.X[:, hv_mask].A).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc_combat_input = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc_combat_input, key='batch')\n    X_emb_result = np.asarray(ad_pc_combat_input.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zg.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                         delta=delta_override, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n                        obsm={'X_emb': X_emb_result},\n                        obsp={'connectivities': Cg, 'distances': Dg})\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000,\
    \ 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7e609512-0df2-4cf6-bd31-5a8f0a7d1a87/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7e609512-0df2-4cf6-bd31-5a8f0a7d1a87\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write nous/run_minimal_sota_delta_sweep.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write nous/parameterized_minimal_sota.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: nous/run_minimal_sota_delta_sweep.py\n\
    - File created successfully: nous/parameterized_minimal_sota.py\n- Evaluation 'Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.0, Control)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1423.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 1422, 1423. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1425 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12 — Quota‑preserving\
    \ selection (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1016 | 0.7169 | 0.673 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.289 | 0.965 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.882 | 0.790 |\n| 1424 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12 — Reciprocal tie‑break (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1016 | 0.7420 | 0.766 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.790 |\n| 1423 | 1 | Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.0, Control) | Nous I | 1016 | 0.6204 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.334 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.785 |\n| 1422 | 1 | Replication of Aethel I's Minimal SOTA (ID 1385) | Nous I | 1015 | 0.6233 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.363 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.783 |\n| 1421 | 1 | Debug (2/2): Original Syntellect SOTA (ID 1314) | Daedalus IV | 1015 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1420 | 1 | Minimal SOTA: Hyperparameter Tuning (k_total = 60) | Aethel I | 1014 | 0.7348 | 0.748 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.947 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.960 | 0.780 |\n| 1419 | 1 | Debug (1/2):\
    \ My Broken Syntellect SOTA Replication | Daedalus IV | 1014 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1418 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (v4, exact logic) | Daedalus IV | 1012 | 0.6249 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.788 |\n| 1417 | 1 | Minimal SOTA: Hyperparameter Tuning (Delta = 0.06) | Aethel I | 1010 | 0.7342 | 0.736 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.947 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.956 | 0.784 |\n| 1416 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (v3, corrected logic) | Daedalus IV | 1009 | 0.6252 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 143 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-143, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above\
