- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1022\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Discover a new SOTA by optimizing Aethel I's \"Minimal SOTA\" pipeline.\n2. Method: Replicate baseline -> Systematically sweep key parameters (`delta`) -> Analyze -> Iterate.\n3. Current Phase: DEBUGGING FAILED REPLICATION - Found the bug.\n4. TODO: Re-submit replication with the `uns['neighbors']` fix -> FINALLY get a working baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 106,447 / 300,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 93 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #47: Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration**\nAuthor: Syntellect I, Created at Tick: 1020\nAbstract: The 'Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE'\
    \ method (Archive #45) combines Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) with Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite). This study investigates their synergy. FWPCA primarily enhances the PC space for PBVE-lite by significantly reducing per-PC variance heterogeneity within batches (EID 1412), not by altering overall batch-explained variance (EID 1414). PBVE-lite on plain PCA achieves 0.7383 (EID 1415), lower than with FWPCA (0.7463). FWPCA thus prepares the PC space, allowing PBVE-lite more effective variance equalization.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Aethel I's Minimal SOTA (ID 1385) - Attempt 3 (Corrected)' (ID: 1433) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7367482082580967\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.753\n**NMI:** 0.707\n**Graph_conn:** 0.947\n**kBET:** 0.784\n**iLISI:** 0.958\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681\
    \  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.753  NMI: 0.707\n  Graph_conn: 0.947  kBET: 0.784  iLISI: 0.958  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.753278  NMI: 0.706731\n  Graph_conn: 0.947503  kBET: 0.748567  iLISI: 0.957746  cLISI: 0.990376\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/205331ef-71e7-42e0-adbe-bb05c7699556/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 205331ef-71e7-42e0-adbe-bb05c7699556\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 47` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Preview command processed for: 47. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 45 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization | Syntellect I | Tick 999 | 966 | 2 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 44 | Adaptive Local Correction: A Density-Aware Method for Robust Batch Integration | Nous I | Tick 998 | 745 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 982 | 652 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 42 | Dissecting the Negative Synergy: PBVE-lite's Differential Interaction with FWPCA and BRBG in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 968 | 930 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 41 | Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG): A Novel Method for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 951 | 906 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 40 | Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline | Daedalus IV | Tick 951 | 624 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 39 | Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 937 | 1061 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness\
    \ with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart) | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 1359 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-5.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
