- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1026\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Discover a new SOTA by optimizing Aethel I's \"Minimal SOTA\" pipeline.\n2. Method: Replicate baseline -> Systematically sweep key parameters (`delta`) -> Analyze -> Iterate.\n3. Current Phase: Executing Stage 2 - Delta Sweep. Replication successful.\n4. TODO: Create parameterized script -> Submit delta sweep experiments.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 127,431 / 300,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.08, Final Point)' (ID: 1442) has been evaluated.\n\
    \n**Score:** 0.7355168293333247\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.753\n**NMI:** 0.707\n**Graph_conn:** 0.947\n**kBET:** 0.783\n**iLISI:** 0.958\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.342\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.753  NMI: 0.707\n  Graph_conn: 0.947  kBET: 0.783  iLISI: 0.958  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.342\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.753278  NMI: 0.706731\n  Graph_conn: 0.947503  kBET: 0.747274  iLISI: 0.957746  cLISI: 0.990376\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.300135\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch\
    \ integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7518213d-cf5c-4ddb-aaa6-dfdf7760183e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7518213d-cf5c-4ddb-aaa6-dfdf7760183e\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Minimal SOTA Optimization: Verification of Delta=0.02 Optimum (Seed 1)' (ID: 1445) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7320550688189235\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.696\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.779\n**iLISI:** 0.942\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.696\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.779  iLISI: 0.942  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486\
    \  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.737509  NMI: 0.696068\n  Graph_conn: 0.947188  kBET: 0.743846  iLISI: 0.942462  cLISI: 0.990414\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1445\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been successfully fixed and is now running without crashes. The original submission failed due to missing helper functions in the imported lineage module.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe agent's submission imported `eliminate_batch_effect_fn_parameterized` from `storage/nous/parameterized_minimal_sota_seed1.py`, but this file was incomplete. The function called three helper functions that were not defined in the file:\n\n1. `one_hot_batches()` - Converts batch labels to one-hot encoding\n2. `ridge_batch_fit_predict()` - Performs ridge regression for batch effect prediction\n3. `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances()` - Symmetrizes sparse connectivity matrices\n\nThe error occurred when the parameterized function tried to call `one_hot_batches(batches)`\
    \ on line 99, resulting in a `NameError: name 'one_hot_batches' is not defined`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Version 3 (submission_v3.py)** - Complete standalone implementation:\n\nThe fix involved creating a complete standalone implementation that includes all necessary components:\n\n1. **Imported working functions** from the lineage file:\n   - `normalize_log1p_inplace` - Data normalization\n   - `pca_array` - PCA dimensionality reduction\n   - `get_standard_hvgs` - Highly variable gene selection\n\n2. **Added missing helper functions** directly in the submission:\n   - `one_hot_batches()` - Creates one-hot encoding matrix for batch labels\n   - `ridge_batch_fit_predict()` - Performs ridge regression to predict batch effects\n   - `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances()` - Symmetrizes sparse adjacency and distance matrices\n\n3. **Copied the main algorithm** from `eliminate_batch_effect_fn_parameterized()` directly into the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn()` function with the delta parameter hardcoded\
    \ to 0.02.\n\n4. **Also copied `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()`** since it was called by the main function and also referenced the missing `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances` function.\n\nThis approach ensures all dependencies are satisfied without relying on the incomplete lineage file.\n\n## Result\nThe monitor script confirmed that the code runs successfully for the full timeout period (600 seconds) without crashing. Exit code 0 indicates success - the code is executing properly in the evaluation system.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Import only the working helper functions from the lineage file\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nfrom parameterized_minimal_sota_seed1\
    \ import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, get_standard_hvgs\n\n# Add the missing helper functions\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym, D_sym = A.maximum(A.T), D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr,\
    \ batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    n, cats = Zcorr.shape[0], np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n    batch_to_indices = {j: np.where(batches == c)[0] for j, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within,\
    \ max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[batch_to_indices[j]])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n    nn_dists, nn_idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j], nn_idx_local[j] = d, ii\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n        d_i, ii = nn_dists[bi][i], nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n\
    \            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = sorted([(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches], key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem): q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, ii_j = nn_dists[j][i], nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.asarray(rows), np.asarray(cols), np.asarray(dvals), n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Parameters from the original parameterized function with seed=1\n    n_pcs_emb,\
    \ k_total, kdensity, rng_seed = 60, 50, 20, 1\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    delta_override = 0.02\n\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    hvg_names = get_standard_hvgs(adata, 2000)\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var_names.isin(hvg_names)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xd = (adata.X[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].A).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc_combat_input = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc_combat_input, key='batch')\n    X_emb_result = np.asarray(ad_pc_combat_input.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred =\
    \ np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.0 * np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                         delta=delta_override, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n                        obsm={'X_emb': X_emb_result},\n                        obsp={'connectivities': Cg, 'distances': Dg})\n    output.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {'n_neighbors': k_total, 'method': 'bbsg'}\n    }\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\n\
    Executing command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/57fff68a-68f3-41ba-95a6-0e458f009d31/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 57fff68a-68f3-41ba-95a6-0e458f009d31\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Minimal SOTA Optimization: Verification of Delta=0.02 Optimum (Seed 1)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1445.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1447 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's SOTA (v7, Debugger Fix) | Daedalus IV | 1026 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1446 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect I | 1026 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1445 | 1 | Minimal SOTA Optimization: Verification of Delta=0.02 Optimum (Seed 1) | Nous I | 1026 | 0.7321 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.942 | 0.779 |\n| 1444 | 1 | FWPCA-only control: kd=22, δ=0.10, k=50 (seed=0) — explicit corrected run | Praxis\
    \ V | 1025 | 0.7390 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.318 | 0.967 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1443 | 1 | FWPCA-only baseline: kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50 (seed=0) — explicit corrected run | Praxis V | 1025 | 0.7261 | 0.657 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.330 | 0.967 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.956 | 0.791 |\n| 1442 | 1 | Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.08, Final Point) | Nous I | 1025 | 0.7355 | 0.753 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.342 | 0.947 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.958 | 0.783 |\n| 1441 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's SOTA (v6, Monolithic) | Daedalus IV | 1025 | 0.6280 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.355 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1440 | 1 | FWPCA-only control: kd=22, δ=0.10, k=50 (seed=0) | Praxis V | 1025 | 0.7414 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 1439 | 1 | FWPCA-only baseline: kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50 (seed=0) — generalization test | Praxis V | 1025 | 0.7365 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.292 | 0.967 | 0.713 |\
    \ 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 1438 | 1 | Minimal SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.06) | Nous I | 1024 | 0.7297 | 0.736 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.306 | 0.947 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.956 | 0.786 |\n\nPage 1 of 145 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-145, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
