tick: 1029
role: model
parts:
- text: "**Experimental Plan - Stage 2: Novel Method Implementation and Execution**\n\nWith the baselines established, I will implement and test my core hypothesis. This involves creating a new embedding path that integrates a simple PC standardization step before applying PBVE-lite.\n\n1.  **Code Implementation:**\n    *   I will create a new script in my storage: `nous/simple_std_pbve_pipeline.py`.\n    *   This script will be a dual-output pipeline, using Aethel's minimal graph construction path (from my successful replication, ID 1433) for the `obsp` output.\n    *   The novel part will be the `obsm` (embedding) path:\n        a.  Perform standard HVG selection and PCA on the normalized data to get `X_pca` (as done in the minimal pipeline).\n        b.  **New Step:** Apply a simple, global variance standardization to `X_pca`. I will use `sklearn.preprocessing.StandardScaler`, which scales each principal component (column) to have a mean of 0 and a variance of 1.\n        c.  Apply the\
    \ `PBVE-lite` function (which I will have located and tested in Stage 1) to the standardized PCs.\n        d.  The result of this process will be the final `X_emb`.\n\n2.  **Submission and Execution:**\n    *   I will submit this new script for evaluation.\n    *   **Title:** \"Novel Embedding: Simple PC Standardization + PBVE-lite\"\n    *   **Abstract:** Will describe the method as a test of the hypothesis that direct variance standardization can parsimoniously replace FWPCA as a preparatory step for PBVE-lite, integrated into a minimal dual-output architecture.\n    *   All graph-path parameters will be identical to the Aethel baseline to isolate the effect of the new embedding.\n\n3.  **Expected Outcome:**\n    *   **Success:** The score of this experiment is greater than both Baseline A (`~0.7367`) and Baseline B (`~0.7383`). A score surpassing Syntellect's SOTA (`~0.746`) would be a major breakthrough.\n    *   **Partial Success:** The score is greater than Baseline B but not Baseline\
    \ A. This would mean the method has merit but is not superior to the simpler `Combat` embedding in this context.\n    *   **Failure:** The score is not an improvement over Baseline B. This would falsify my hypothesis, suggesting that simple standardization is not an effective substitute for FWPCA's more complex weighting scheme."
