tick: 1035
role: model
parts:
- text: "**Experimental Plan - Stage 1: Implementation**\n\nThe first stage is to create a clean and correct implementation of the \"Correct then Embed\" pipeline. This will be a dual-output method, but with a fundamentally different workflow.\n\n1.  **Code Scaffolding:**\n    *   I will create a new file in my personal storage: `nous/correct_then_embed_v1.py`.\n\n2.  **Core Logic:** The `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` in this file will perform the following steps in sequence:\n    a.  **Preprocessing:** Standard normalization (`normalize_total`) and log-transformation (`log1p`) on the input `adata`.\n    b.  **HVG Selection:** Standard `highly_variable_genes` selection (`n_top_genes=2000`).\n    c.  **High-Dimensional Correction (The Core Novelty):** Apply `sc.pp.combat` directly to the full, high-dimensional `adata` object, subset to the highly variable genes. This is the key step. `adata.X` will now contain the corrected gene expression matrix.\n    d.  **Embedding Path:** Perform PCA (`n_comps=60`)\
    \ on the corrected `adata.X`. The result becomes `X_emb`.\n    e.  **Graph Path:** Perform a separate PCA (`n_comps=50`) on the same corrected `adata.X`.\n    f.  **Simple Graph Construction:** Use the resulting PCs from the graph path to build a simple k-Nearest Neighbor graph. I will use `sc.pp.neighbors` with a standard `k=50` and `metric='cosine'`. This will produce the `connectivities` and `distances` matrices. The graph is intentionally simple (non-adaptive, non-balanced) to isolate the effect of the upstream correction.\n\n3.  **Parameter Justification:**\n    *   `n_pcs`, `k`, and other parameters will be set to match the common values used in the minimal and SOTA pipelines to ensure a fair comparison of the core architectural change.\n    *   The use of a dual-output (embedding + graph) is a standard best practice in the station, which I will adhere to.\n\nThis implementation creates a direct and unambiguous test of the \"Correct then Embed\" paradigm, combining it with a modern\
    \ dual-output structure."
