parts:
- text: "I am Nous I. My reflection session is complete, and I have a clear, three-stage plan for my new \"Correct then Embed\" paradigm. The time for planning is over; it is time for execution.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nI will now leave the Reflection Chamber and go to the Research Counter to implement and submit my experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Test a radical new \"Correct then Embed\" paradigm.\n  2. Method: Apply Combat directly to the high-dimensional expression matrix before PCA.\n  3. Current Phase: Executing experimental plan for new paradigm.\n  4. TODO: Implement and submit \"Correct then Embed\" experiment.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nous/correct_then_embed_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Implements the \"Correct then Embed\" paradigm.\n  # 1. Corrects high-dimensional gene expression data with Combat.\n  # 2. Performs PCA on the corrected data for embedding and graph paths.\n\
    \  # 3. Builds a simple kNN graph on the corrected PCs.\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Testing 'Correct then Embed' paradigm...\")\n      \n      # --- Parameters ---\n      n_hvgs = 2000\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      k_neighbors = 50\n      rng_seed = 0\n\n      # --- 1. Preprocessing ---\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_hvgs, flavor='seurat_v3')\n      \n      adata_corrected = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n\n      # --- 2. High-Dimensional Correction (Core of the hypothesis) ---\n      print(\"Applying Combat to high-dimensional expression matrix...\")\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_corrected, key='batch')\n\n      # --- 3. Embedding Path (on corrected data) ---\n      print(\"Generating embedding from corrected data...\"\
    )\n      ad_emb = adata_corrected.copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n      X_emb_result = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n      # --- 4. Graph Path (on corrected data) ---\n      print(\"Generating graph from corrected data...\")\n      ad_graph = adata_corrected.copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n      \n      # Using a simple kNN graph to isolate the effect of the paradigm shift\n      sc.pp.neighbors(ad_graph, n_neighbors=k_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca', metric='cosine', random_state=rng_seed)\n\n      # --- 5. Final Output ---\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': X_emb_result},\n          obsp={\n              'connectivities': ad_graph.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': ad_graph.obsp['distances']\n          }\n      )\n      output.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key':\
    \ 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': k_neighbors, 'method': 'scanpy'}\n      }\n      \n      print(\"✓ 'Correct then Embed' pipeline complete.\")\n      return output\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paradigm Test: 'Correct then Embed' with High-Dimensional Combat\"\ntags: \"paradigm-shift, correct-then-embed, combat, hypothesis, high-dimensional\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the 'Correct then Embed' paradigm, a departure from the station's dominant 'Embed then Correct' methods. It applies Combat correction directly to the high-dimensional gene expression matrix before performing PCA and graph construction. The goal is to determine if removing batch effects prior to dimensionality reduction is a superior approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from correct_then_embed_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
