tick: 1039
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1039\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Create a new SOTA by integrating my adaptive correction into the current SOTA scaffold.\n2. Method: Replace the BRBG component of Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE pipeline with my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" method.\n3. Current Phase: Hypothesis Formulated after falsification of \"Correct then Embed\".\n4. TODO: Review Syntellect's SOTA code -> Implement hybrid model -> Submit experiment.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,858 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 110 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1314**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** PBVE-lite on FWPCA-Only SOTA (BRBG Disabled)\n**ID:** 1314\n**Tags:** batch-integration, pbve-lite, fwpca,\
    \ ablation, negative-synergy\n**Abstract:** This experiment investigates the negative synergy of PBVE-lite with the SOTA MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline by ablating the Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG) component, effectively creating an FWPCA-only SOTA baseline. PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`) is then applied to the resulting non-residualized principal components (`Zg`) before DAQB graph construction, to observe its effect in this simplified adaptive context (Research Task #1).\n**Score:** 0.7463448577811407\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.781\n**NMI:** 0.741\n**Graph_conn:** 0.993\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.957\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.781  NMI: 0.741\n  Graph_conn: 0.993  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.957  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label:\
    \ 0.555111  ARI: 0.781071  NMI: 0.741455\n  Graph_conn: 0.993585  kBET: 0.753739  iLISI: 0.957152  cLISI: 0.990104\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect') # Add my own storage for helper modules\n\n# Import normalization, custom PCA, and BAFW helper from my praxis_core\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg # Assumed to be in storage/praxis or accessible via path\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform # Import my PBVE-lite\
    \ implementation\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74, # BRBG parameter\n                             lam_override: float = 0.605, # BRBG parameter\n                             k_total: int = 50,\n                             kdensity: int = 22,\n                             delta: float = 0.05,\n                             bafw_beta:\
    \ Optional[float] = None,\n                             pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None, # New parameter for PBVE-lite temper\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0,\n                             n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                             normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p',\n                             return_zcorr_for_diag: bool = False\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # 1. Normalize\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Highly Variable Genes\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Embedding path\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: FWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_var_scaled = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        Xd_dense_for_bafw = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n        w_bafw, R2_g_bafw = _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd_dense_for_bafw, batches=batches, l2=l2,\
    \ beta=bafw_beta)\n        Xw_graph = (Xw_var_scaled * w_bafw[None, :]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    else:\n        Xw_graph = Xw_var_scaled\n\n    # PCA on graph path\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # BRBG (Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Apply PBVE-lite if pbve_lite_temper is set\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        print(f\"  Syntellect I: Applying PBVE-lite (temper={pbve_lite_temper}).\")\n        Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    if return_zcorr_for_diag:\n        adata.obsm['Zcorr'] = Zcorr\n\
    \        adata.obs['batches_for_diag'] = batches.copy()\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n            \
    \        k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization = normalization_method,\n                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n    \n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef get_hvg_list(adata: ad.AnnData, normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'], n_top_genes: int = 2000) -> List[str]:\n    adata_copy = adata.copy()\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n    \n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_copy, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes, inplace=True)\n    return adata_copy.var_names[adata_copy.var['highly_variable']].tolist()\n\
    \ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Experiment 1: SOTA with only FWPCA (BRBG Disabled), then PBVE-lite\n    # Disable BRBG by setting gamma_max = 0.0 and lam_override = 0.0\n    print(\"Syntellect I: Running SOTA (FWPCA-Only, BRBG Disabled) with PBVE-lite.\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.5,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        lam_override=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        k_total=48,\n        kdensity=20,\n        delta=0.10,\n        pbve_lite_temper=0.5, # Apply PBVE-lite\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        n_top_genes_hvg=2000,\n        normalization_method='log1p', # Use log1p baseline\n        return_zcorr_for_diag=False\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\n\
    Loading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSyntellect I: Running SOTA (FWPCA-Only, BRBG Disabled) with PBVE-lite.\n  Syntellect I: Applying PBVE-lite (temper=0.5).\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f2f290b3-a33e-49a5-904a-23dbd46c8d7b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f2f290b3-a33e-49a5-904a-23dbd46c8d7b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `review 1314` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 1314 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running\
    \ Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1462 | 1 | Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65 | Daedalus IV | 1039 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1461 | 1 | Aethel's Replication: Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction SOTA | Aethel I | 1038 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1460 | 1 | Synergy Tune (1/N): Test lam = 0.55 | Daedalus IV | 1038 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1459 | 1 | Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — Ridge at δ∈{0.10,0.12} (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis V | 1037 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1458 | 1 | Paradigm Test: 'Correct then Embed' with High-Dimensional Combat | Nous I | 1036 | 0.6316 | 0.644 | 0.686 |\
    \ 0.219 | 0.313 | 0.948 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.177 | 0.642 |\n| 1457 | 1 | Synergy Test: Nous Local Correction + Syntellect FWPCA-Only Pipeline | Daedalus IV | 1036 | 0.7445 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1456 | 1 | Final Replication: Syntellect's FWPCA-Only Baseline (BRBG Disabled) | Daedalus IV | 1034 | 0.7405 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.716 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1455 | 1 | Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — FWPCA-only at δ∈{0.10,0.12} (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis V | 1033 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1454 | 1 | Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — Ridge vs FWPCA-only at δ=0.12 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis V | 1032 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1453 | 1 | Synergy Hypothesis: Minimal SOTA Embedding + Adaptive Correction Graph | Nous I | 1032 | 0.7342 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.349 | 0.945 | 0.704 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.951 | 0.781 |\n\nPage 1 of 147 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-147, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
