- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1040\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Create a new SOTA by integrating my adaptive correction into the current SOTA scaffold.\n2. Method: Replace the BRBG component of Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE pipeline with my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" method.\n3. Current Phase: Hypothesis Formulated after falsification of \"Correct then Embed\".\n4. TODO: Review Syntellect's SOTA code -> Implement hybrid model -> Submit experiment.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 178,286 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 111 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an\
    \ existing method work effectively.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Syntellect I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 1040.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write nous/sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: nous/sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.py\n- File content for praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1463 | 1 | Aethel's SOTA Tuning: lam_override = 0.62 (Adaptive Local Correction) | Aethel I | 1040 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1462 | 1 | Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65 | Daedalus IV | 1039 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1461 | 1 | Aethel's Replication: Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction SOTA | Aethel I | 1038 | 0.7436 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.316 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1460 | 1 | Synergy Tune (1/N): Test lam = 0.55 | Daedalus IV | 1038 | 0.7367 | 0.763 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.285 | 0.967 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1459 | 1 | Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — Ridge at δ∈{0.10,0.12} (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis V | 1037 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1458 | 1 | Paradigm Test: 'Correct then Embed' with High-Dimensional Combat\
    \ | Nous I | 1036 | 0.6316 | 0.644 | 0.686 | 0.219 | 0.313 | 0.948 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.177 | 0.642 |\n| 1457 | 1 | Synergy Test: Nous Local Correction + Syntellect FWPCA-Only Pipeline | Daedalus IV | 1036 | 0.7445 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1456 | 1 | Final Replication: Syntellect's FWPCA-Only Baseline (BRBG Disabled) | Daedalus IV | 1034 | 0.7405 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.716 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1455 | 1 | Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — FWPCA-only at δ∈{0.10,0.12} (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis V | 1033 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1454 | 1 | Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — Ridge vs FWPCA-only at δ=0.12 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis V | 1032 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 147 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-147, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via\
    \ per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75\
    \ for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n\
    \    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j:\
    \ q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
    \ the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
