- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1042\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Create a new SOTA by integrating my adaptive correction into the current SOTA scaffold.\n2. Method: Replace the BRBG component of Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE pipeline with my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" method.\n3. Current Phase: Hypothesis Formulated after falsification of \"Correct then Embed\".\n4. TODO: Review Syntellect's SOTA code -> Implement hybrid model -> Submit experiment.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 190,163 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 113 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Hypothesis v2: Adaptive Correction on FWPCA-Combat Scaffold' (ID: 1464) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6094148260509826\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.444\n**NMI:** 0.679\n**Graph_conn:** 0.935\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.020\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.444  NMI: 0.679\n  Graph_conn: 0.935  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.020  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.443690  NMI: 0.678709\n  Graph_conn: 0.936576  kBET: 0.752632  iLISI: 0.019769  cLISI: 0.998072\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1464\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in submission v2. The submission is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (evaluation 1464) failed with a `NameError: name 'PCA' is not defined` error at line 23 in the `pca_array_custom` function within `storage/nous/sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.py`.\n\
    \nThe function was attempting to use `PCA` from scikit-learn, but the import statement was missing. The lineage file only imported `NearestNeighbors` from sklearn but forgot to import `PCA` from `sklearn.decomposition`.\n\n**Error traceback:**\n```\nFile \"/tmp/tmpj2hgntv2/storage/nous/sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.py\", line 23, in pca_array_custom\n    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n          ^^^\nNameError: name 'PCA' is not defined. Did you mean: 'pca'?\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following approach:\n\n1. **Added the missing import**: Imported `PCA` from `sklearn.decomposition`\n2. **Copied the buggy function**: Copied only the `pca_array_custom` function from the lineage file\n3. **Fixed the function**: The copied version now has access to the `PCA` import\n4. **Monkey-patched the module**: Used Python's dynamic nature to replace the buggy function in the imported module with the fixed\
    \ version\n5. **Preserved other imports**: Kept importing the main `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` and other working helper functions from the lineage file\n\nThis approach follows best practices:\n- Only copied the broken function (not the entire file)\n- Kept all other working functions as imports\n- Minimal changes to fix the specific bug\n\n## Result\nThe submission v2 ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming the fix resolved the import error. The code is executing the batch integration algorithm as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\n\n# Import the main function and other working helpers\nfrom sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction import (\n    eliminate_batch_effect_fn,\n\
    \    normalize_total_log1p_inplace,\n    one_hot_batches,\n    ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _fw_weight_by_var,\n    build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n)\n\n# Fix the buggy pca_array_custom function by copying it here with the missing import\ndef pca_array_custom(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return pca.fit_transform(Xd)\n\n# Monkey-patch the fixed function back into the module\nimport sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction\nsota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.pca_array_custom = pca_array_custom\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nNous I: Testing Adaptive Local Correction on FWPCA SOTA scaffold.\n  Nous I:\
    \ Applying Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8a731070-4c2d-43a0-85d5-f6864c59e94b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8a731070-4c2d-43a0-85d5-f6864c59e94b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write nous/sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: nous/sota_scaffold_adaptive_correction.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label |\
