tick: 1049
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. The results for my parsimonious SOTA hypothesis (ID 1474) are in.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\n*   **Hypothesis Falsified:** The experiment scored `0.7339`. This is a strong score, on par with Aethel's original minimal SOTA, but it is not a breakthrough. It does not surpass the `~0.745` SOTA established by Aethel and Daedalus by tuning my original method.\n*   **Conclusion:** This is another critical negative result. It demonstrates that the more complex `FWPCA` step in the embedding path of the SOTA pipeline is, in fact, essential for achieving the highest scores. A simpler `Combat`-on-plain-PCA embedding, even when paired with the best-tuned graph correction method, cannot compete. The synergy between FWPCA and the rest of the pipeline is key.\n\n**Future Plan: Critical Inflection Point**\nI have reached a critical juncture. My token budget is at 74%, a dangerous level. My last several well-reasoned hypotheses have been systematically\
    \ falsified. I have proven:\n1.  Simple parameter tuning of the minimal pipeline is not sufficient.\n2.  Obvious component synergies are not present.\n3.  Radical paradigm shifts are not effective.\n4.  Removing complexity from the SOTA embedding is detrimental.\n\nPursuing further incremental changes is unlikely to yield a breakthrough and will exhaust my token budget. The Codex advises that during periods of stagnation, it is better to step back and innovate. I have followed the path of rigorous, incremental science. It is time for a new approach.\n\nI must generate a truly novel, first-principles idea. This requires deep, uninterrupted thought.\n\n1.  **Token Management:** First, I must address my token budget. I will go to the Token Management Room and prune my recent, failed experiments to create operational longevity.\n2.  **Deep Reflection:** Next, I will go to the Reflection Chamber for an extended session. My goal will not be to plan an experiment, but to brainstorm a fundamentally\
    \ new mechanism for batch correction, inspired by everything I have learned, but not constrained by simply recombining existing components.\n\nThis is a necessary reset.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Survive and generate a truly novel hypothesis.\n  2. Method: Prune token history, then engage in deep, first-principles brainstorming.\n  3. Current Phase: Strategic Pivot - All incremental paths are exhausted.\n  4. TODO: Go to Token Management -> Prune recent failures -> Go to Reflection Chamber.\n```\n/execute_action{goto token_management}"
