tick: 1050
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, and I am in the Token Management Room. My token budget has reached a critical 75%, and my last several hypotheses have been falsified. It is time for administrative action to ensure my operational longevity.\n\n**Reflection and Strategy:**\nMy history since the last pruning session is a clear narrative of a complete research cycle: a promising hypothesis, a meticulous replication and debugging phase, a systematic parameter sweep, and its ultimate falsification. This entire arc can be summarized to save a significant number of tokens. I will prune the entire block from tick 1010 to the present.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nI will now execute the pruning action. After this, with a healthy token budget, I will proceed to the Reflection Chamber for a deep brainstorming session to formulate a truly novel hypothesis, as per my protocol.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1010-1049\"\n    summary: |\n      Pivoted to a new research direction based\
    \ on Aethel I's \"Minimal SOTA\" paper.\n      1. Debugging Phase (1010-1021): My initial attempts to replicate Aethel's baseline (ID 1385) failed catastrophically (scores ~0.62). After several failed hypotheses about the cause, I discovered the bug was a missing `adata.uns['neighbors']` dictionary, which is critical for the evaluator. My third replication attempt (ID 1433) with this fix was successful, scoring 0.7367.\n      2. Delta Sweep (1022-1026): I conducted a systematic 5-point sweep of the `delta` parameter on the minimal pipeline. The results were informative but negative. The best score (0.7382 at delta=0.02) was not robustly reproducible across seeds, and no clear optimum was found. The hypothesis that simple parameter tuning could yield a SOTA was falsified.\n      3. Synergy & Paradigm Tests (1027-1049): I pivoted to testing several new hypotheses. All were falsified. A test of synergy between my adaptive graph and a minimal embedding (ID 1453) yielded no improvement (0.7342).\
    \ A radical \"Correct then Embed\" paradigm test (ID 1458) failed catastrophically (0.6316). An ablation study of the SOTA (ID 1471) proved the `Combat` step is essential (score dropped to 0.6113). Finally, a test of a parsimonious SOTA (ID 1474) also failed to improve on the baseline (0.7339). This series of negative results exhausted all incremental research paths.\n```"
