- text: "I am Nous I, and my deep reflection session in the Reflection Chamber is now complete. I have formulated a novel, first-principles hypothesis centered on Independent Component Analysis (ICA) and a component falsification strategy. The full experimental plan, including a crucial control baseline, is ready.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe planning phase is over. It is time for execution. My protocol must be updated to reflect this transition from brainstorming to active experimentation. The next steps are clear and sequential: update my status, move to the research counter, and begin implementing the two-pronged experiment.\n\n**Future Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** I will set my new protocol, clearly stating the \"ICA-Falsification\" hypothesis and the two-submission plan.\n2.  **Navigate:** I will go to the Research Counter.\n3.  **Implement Control:** I will immediately write and submit the simple, uncorrected PCA baseline. This is a quick task that will establish the control group\
    \ for my main experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Test the novel \"ICA-Falsification\" paradigm.\n  2. Method: Execute a two-part experiment: a simple PCA baseline as a control, and the full ICA-Falsification method as the test.\n  3. Current Phase: Execution.\n  4. TODO: Submit control baseline -> Submit ICA test -> Analyze results.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline: Simple Uncorrected PCA Embedding (50 comps)\"\ntags: \"ica-falsification-series, baseline, pca, no-correction\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission serves as the control baseline for the ICA-Falsification hypothesis. It applies a standard PCA with 50 components to the log-normalized data and returns the embedding without any batch correction. This provides a \"do-nothing\" benchmark against which the experimental method can be fairly compared.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Control baseline: Simple PCA embedding with no correction.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Standard preprocessing\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # Uncorrected PCA embedding\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n\n      # The embedding is stored in adata.obsm['X_pca'] by default.\n      # We will return this directly.\n      # For consistency with expected output format, copy it to 'X_emb'\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      return adata\n```"
