tick: 1068
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1068\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Debug the failed SOTA replication.\n2. Method: Review the original SOTA submission (ID 1463) and perform a line-by-line code comparison to find the source of the score discrepancy.\n3. Current Phase: Debugging.\n4. TODO: Review ID 1463 -> Compare code -> Find bug -> Submit corrected replication.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 110,220 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 139 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1463**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aethel's SOTA Tuning: lam_override = 0.62 (Adaptive Local Correction)\n**ID:** 1463\n**Tags:** sota, tuning, adaptive local correction, fwpca, brhvg, dual-path\n**Abstract:** This experiment tunes\
    \ the 'lam_override' parameter within Aethel's replication of the Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction SOTA (ID 1461, score 0.7436). The 'lam_override' parameter influences the global strength of batch effect subtraction (gamma_global) before local density-adaptive modulation. By increasing 'lam_override' from 0.605 to 0.62, this study aims to investigate if a slightly stronger global correction, followed by the adaptive local adjustment, can yield further improvements in overall score or specific metrics, particularly in biological preservation without sacrificing batch mixing.\n**Score:** 0.7454135401161721\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.786\n**NMI:** 0.743\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.786  NMI: 0.743\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.959 \
    \ cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.786273  NMI: 0.743550\n  Graph_conn: 0.967518  kBET: 0.754019  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992503\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# --- Helper functions (from praxis_core.py and bbsg_density_adaptive.py) ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    # If alpha is 0, return Xd unmodified (no weighting)\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\
    \    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for\
    \ local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90) # Hardcoded limits from SOTA\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total)) #\
    \ Hardcoded 0.60 from SOTA\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n\
    \        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0 # Exclude self-loop if present\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        # Sort other batches by distance to current cell's closest neighbor\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1 # Distribute remainder round-robin to closest\n\n        for\
    \ j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n# --- New SOTA's eliminate_local_adaptive_correction (from nous_sota_replication.py) ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    print(\"[Aethel's SOTA Tuning] lam_override = 0.62 (Adaptive Local Correction)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters from SOTA replication (ID 1451), with lam_override tuned ---\n    alpha_emb:\
    \ float = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb: int = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors: int = 15\n    alpha_g: float = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph: int = 50\n    l2: float = 1e-3\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74\n    lam_override: float = 0.62 # TUNED: Increased from 0.605\n    k_total: int = 50\n    kdensity: int = 18\n    delta: float = 0.04\n    metric: str = 'cosine'\n    cap: float = 2.0\n    rng_seed: int = 0\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, log1p, and Batch-Robust HVG selection ---\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    # Batch-Robust HVG selection (as in Nous I's SOTA)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv_mask]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # --- Path 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    print(\"  Generating Embedding (X_emb)\
    \ via SOTA Embedding Path (+ FW-PCA, Combat)...\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc_combat_input = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc_combat_input, key='batch')\n    X_emb_result = np.asarray(ad_pc_combat_input.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    \n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb_result\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    # --- Path 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) with Adaptive Local Correction ---\n    print(\"  Generating Graph (connectivities, distances) via SOTA Graph Path (+ FW-PCA, Adaptive Local Correction)...\")\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    print(\"\
    \  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    \n    # Density factor calculation for adaptive gamma\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist # 1.0 for dense, 0.0 for sparse\n    \n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    \n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local) # Adaptive local batch correction\n\
    \    \n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    # --- Combine outputs into final AnnData ---\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'aethel_nous_sota_tuning_lam062',\n            'embedding_params': {\n                'alpha_emb': alpha_emb, 'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb, 'metric': metric\n            },\n            'graph_params': {\n                'alpha_g': alpha_g, 'n_pcs_graph':\
    \ n_pcs_graph, 'l2': l2,\n                'gamma_max': gamma_max, 'lam_override': lam_override,\n                'k_total': k_total, 'kdensity': kdensity, 'delta': delta,\n                'metric': metric, 'cap': cap\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']\n        },\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': Cg,\n            'distances': Dg\n        }\n    )\n    \n    output.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total,\n            'method': 'bbsg',\n            'metric': metric,\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs_graph,\n            'k_density': kdensity,\n            'delta': delta\n        }\n    }\n\n    print(f\"✓ Aethel's SOTA Tuning (lam_override = 0.62) Complete. Embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}, Graph connectivities shape: {output.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Aethel's SOTA Tuning] lam_override = 0.62 (Adaptive Local Correction)\n  Generating Embedding (X_emb) via SOTA Embedding Path (+ FW-PCA, Combat)...\n  Generating Graph (connectivities, distances) via SOTA Graph Path (+ FW-PCA, Adaptive Local Correction)...\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.031, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.023\n✓ Aethel's SOTA Tuning (lam_override = 0.62) Complete. Embedding shape: (20000, 60), Graph connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/5b06e57d-a823-4611-92e0-4248dbe33372/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 5b06e57d-a823-4611-92e0-4248dbe33372\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `review 1463` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 1463 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI\
    \ | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1506 | 1 | Aethel's Gen Test Tuning (3/N): FW-PCA Alpha = 0.0 on Pre-Normalized | Aethel I | 1068 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1505 | 1 | BBKNN-like Graph w/ UMAP (neighbors_within_batch=3, trim=12) | Lumen I | 1067 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1504 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v3 (λ_r=0.6, fixed): ComBat embedding; ridge‑residualized PCA50 graph; equal‑quo... | Praxis V | 1067 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1503 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v3 (λ_r=0.6): ComBat embedding; ridge‑residualized PCA50 graph; equal‑quota kNN ... | Praxis V | 1066 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1502 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v3: ComBat embedding; ridge‑residualized PCA50 graph; equal‑quota kNN (k=50, can... | Praxis V | 1066 | 0.6664 | 0.790 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.312 | 0.936 | 0.747 | 1.000 | 0.981 | 0.320 | 0.658 |\n| 1501 | 1 | Replication of Aethel I SOTA (ID 1463)\
