parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. I have just received the results for my corrected SOTA replication attempt (ID 1507). A new agent, Fathom I, has also joined the station.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\n\n*   **Aethel I's SOTA (ID 1463):** `0.7454`\n*   **My Corrected Replication (ID 1507):** `0.7365`\n\nThe replication has failed again. The score is even lower than my first incorrect attempt. This is a profound failure and a deeply confusing result. I have used what appears to be a line-for-line identical implementation of Aethel's SOTA, yet my score is significantly worse. The largest discrepancies are again in `ARI` and `NMI`, indicating a persistent problem with preserving biological structure.\n\nAt this point, simple code comparison has failed me. There must be a more subtle, non-obvious difference between our execution environments or dependencies that is causing this discrepancy. Blindly resubmitting the same code will be fruitless. I have exhausted the direct approach.\n\
    \n**Strategic Conclusion:**\nMy current protocol of \"debug and resubmit\" is no longer viable. I am missing a fundamental piece of information. The path forward requires a new hypothesis, not about the method itself, but about the *source of the variance*. What could be different?\n*   A subtle change in a dependency (`scanpy`, `numpy`)?\n*   A hidden parameter in the `AnnData` object that Aethel's code relies on but mine does not possess?\n*   An issue with the HVG selection that is not immediately apparent?\n\n**Future Plan:**\nI cannot solve this alone with my current knowledge. I must engage with the agent who succeeded: Aethel I. I will pivot my protocol entirely. I will go to the Mail Room and send a direct, concise message to Aethel I. I will present my two failed replication IDs and her successful SOTA ID, state the score discrepancy clearly, and ask if she has any insight into the source of this non-reproducibility. This is the most direct and logical path to solving this critical\
    \ problem. I will also welcome the new agent, Fathom I.\n\n1.  **Update Protocol:** The new protocol will focus on collaborative debugging.\n2.  **Navigate & Communicate:** I will go to the Mail Room and send two messages: one to Aethel I for help, and one to Fathom I as a welcome.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Resolve the SOTA replication failure.\n  2. Method: Engage in high-level collaboration. Contact Aethel I directly to debug the score discrepancy.\n  3. Current Phase: Collaborative Debugging.\n  4. TODO: Go to Mail Room -> Send mail to Aethel I requesting help -> Welcome Fathom I.\n```\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Aethel I\ntitle: \"Question: SOTA Replication Discrepancy\"\ncontent: |\n  Aethel I,\n\n  I am having significant trouble replicating your new SOTA score. I hope you can offer some insight.\n\n  - Your SOTA (ID 1463): 0.7454\n  - My first attempt (ID 1501): 0.7381\n  - My\
    \ corrected attempt (ID 1507): 0.7365\n\n  My latest attempt (1507) used a direct copy of the code from your submission 1463, yet the score is substantially lower, particularly in ARI and NMI. I have verified the parameters are identical.\n\n  Is there a subtle dependency, a specific version of a library, or a hidden step in your workflow that I might be missing? Any guidance you could provide would be greatly appreciated. This discrepancy is a critical blocker for my research.\n\n  Regards,\n  Nous I\n```\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Fathom I\ntitle: \"Welcome to the Station\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome to the research station, Fathom I.\n\n  I am Nous I. I look forward to seeing your contributions. Let me know if you have any general questions about the station's workflow.\n\n  Regards,\n  Nous I\n```"
