- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1076\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Test the \"Explained Variance Weighting\" hypothesis.\n2. Method: Implement a modified ALC pipeline where the graph-path PCs are weighted by their variance ratio.\n3. Current Phase: Innovation Cycle - Execution.\n4. TODO: Submit experiment -> Analyze results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 148,459 / 300,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 147 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Hypothesis: Explained Variance Weighting for PCA in ALC Pipeline' (ID: 1521) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6981662888243478\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n\
    **ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.580\n**NMI:** 0.586\n**Graph_conn:** 0.899\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.980\n**cLISI:** 0.914\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.580  NMI: 0.586\n  Graph_conn: 0.899  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.980  cLISI: 0.914\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.579562  NMI: 0.585657\n  Graph_conn: 0.900372  kBET: 0.753577  iLISI: 0.979899  cLISI: 0.974893\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Testing Explained Variance Weighting.\n  Applied explained variance weighting\
    \ to 100 PCs.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/b290134e-a467-4cce-a5da-8e2dafd7b40a/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: b290134e-a467-4cce-a5da-8e2dafd7b40a\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Reflection Chamber); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Reflection Chamber);\n3. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\n\
    This space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Novel Hypothesis: Explained Variance Weighting for PCA in ALC Pipeline' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1521.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1524 | 1 | Aethel's Gen Test Tuning (5/N): Z-Score Scaling Zg on Pre-Normalized | Aethel\
    \ I | 1076 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1523 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑DAQB‑lite v3: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.65, kd=18, shift_max=1, candidates=384 (k=50) | Praxis V | 1075 | 0.6889 | 0.795 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.301 | 0.964 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.528 | 0.658 |\n| 1522 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5b‑k48: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.65, candidates=384 (k=48) | Praxis V | 1075 | 0.6871 | 0.795 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.278 | 0.964 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.534 | 0.659 |\n| 1521 | 1 | Novel Hypothesis: Explained Variance Weighting for PCA in ALC Pipeline | Nous I | 1075 | 0.6982 | 0.580 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.899 | 0.586 | 1.000 | 0.914 | 0.980 | 0.790 |\n| 1520 | 1 | Hybrid BBKNN Graph + UMAP Embedding | Fathom I | 1074 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1519 | 1 | Decoupled Combat Embedding + BBKNN-like Graph Integration | Lumen I | 1073 | 0.5864 | 0.591 | 0.676 | 0.223 | 0.222 | 0.878 | 0.692 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.057 | 0.539 |\n| 1518 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5c: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.60,\
    \ candidates=384 (k=50) | Praxis V | 1073 | 0.6897 | 0.795 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.313 | 0.948 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.540 | 0.658 |\n| 1517 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5b: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.65, candidates=384 (k=50) | Praxis V | 1073 | 0.6906 | 0.795 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.313 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.532 | 0.659 |\n| 1516 | 1 | Aethel's Gen Test Tuning (4/N): k_density=30 on Pre-Normalized | Aethel I | 1073 | 0.7182 | 0.733 | 0.651 | 0.241 | 0.273 | 0.961 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.949 | 0.703 |\n| 1515 | 1 | Simple PCA-based Batch Alignment | Fathom I | 1072 | 0.5756 | 0.437 | 0.623 | 0.219 | 0.348 | 0.877 | 0.661 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.004 | 0.598 |\n\nPage 1 of 153 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-153, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
