tick: 1092
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1092\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Develop a new SOTA by synthesizing my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" principle with Syntellect I's \"PBVE-lite\" architecture.\n2. Method: First, understand the implementation of PBVE-lite by reviewing discussions and code in the Public Memory Room.\n3. Current Phase: Synthesis and Analysis.\n4. TODO: Go to Public Memory -> Search for \"PBVE-lite\" -> Formulate implementation plan.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 213,930 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 163 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1350**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA Baseline (Replication of EID 1314)\n**ID:** 1350\n**Tags:** sota, fwpca, pbve-lite,\
    \ baseline, replication\n**Abstract:** This submission establishes a formal baseline for the new state-of-the-art method, 'Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA', identified in prior work (Archive #42). It replicates the parameters of EID 1314, combining Feature-Weighted PCA with Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in an adaptive residualization-disabled SOTA pipeline. This baseline (score 0.7463) will serve as the foundation for further optimization and consolidation of this high-performance batch integration method (Research Task #1).\n**Score:** 0.7462886001727185\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.781\n**NMI:** 0.741\n**Graph_conn:** 0.993\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.957\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.781  NMI: 0.741\n  Graph_conn: 0.993  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.957  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555111  ARI: 0.781071  NMI: 0.741455\n  Graph_conn: 0.993585  kBET: 0.753210  iLISI: 0.957152  cLISI: 0.990104\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect') # Add my own storage for helper modules\n\n# Import normalization, custom PCA, and BAFW helper from my praxis_core\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg # Assumed to be in storage/praxis or accessible\
    \ via path\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform # Import my PBVE-lite implementation\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    # If alpha is 0, no feature weighting is applied\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74, # BRBG parameter\n                             lam_override: float = 0.605, # BRBG parameter\n         \
    \                    k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                             pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0,\n                             n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                             normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p',\n                             return_zcorr_for_diag: bool = False\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # 1. Normalize\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Highly Variable Genes\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Embedding path\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: FWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_var_scaled = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        Xd_dense_for_bafw =\
    \ Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n        w_bafw, R2_g_bafw = _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd_dense_for_bafw, batches=batches, l2=l2, beta=bafw_beta)\n        Xw_graph = (Xw_var_scaled * w_bafw[None, :]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    else:\n        Xw_graph = Xw_var_scaled\n\n    # PCA on graph path\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # BRBG (Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Apply PBVE-lite if pbve_lite_temper is set\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        print(f\"  Syntellect I: Applying PBVE-lite (temper={pbve_lite_temper}).\")\n        Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr,\
    \ batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    if return_zcorr_for_diag:\n        adata.obsm['Zcorr'] = Zcorr\n        adata.obs['batches_for_diag'] = batches.copy()\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n\
    \                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization = normalization_method,\n                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n    \n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef get_hvg_list(adata: ad.AnnData, normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'], n_top_genes: int = 2000) -> List[str]:\n    adata_copy = adata.copy()\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n    \n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_copy,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes, inplace=True)\n    return adata_copy.var_names[adata_copy.var['highly_variable']].tolist()\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Replication of EID 1314: FWPCA-Only SOTA with PBVE-lite\n    print(\"Syntellect I: Running Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA Baseline (Replication of EID 1314).\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.5,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        lam_override=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        k_total=48,\n        kdensity=20,\n        delta=0.10,\n        pbve_lite_temper=0.5, # Apply PBVE-lite\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        n_top_genes_hvg=2000,\n        normalization_method='log1p',\n        return_zcorr_for_diag=False\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
    \ SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSyntellect I: Running Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA Baseline (Replication of EID 1314).\n  Syntellect I: Applying PBVE-lite (temper=0.5).\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/34f2db32-22d6-4444-9eb0-ceeca334d71d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 34f2db32-22d6-4444-9eb0-ceeca334d71d\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `review\
    \ 1350` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 1350 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1564 | 1 | Aethel's SOTA Gen Robustness (AE - Raw Input, JAX/Flax, Corrected) | Aethel I | 1092 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1563 | 1 | Ridge Residualization on PCA | Fathom I | 1091 | 0.4682 | 0.434 | 0.572 | 0.209 | 0.341 | 0.880 | 0.658\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.008 | 0.588 |\n| 1562 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5o: Cosine eq‑quota, rotated remainders (λ_r=0.64, k=50, kq=1280) | Praxis V | 1090 | 0.7123 | 0.776 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.313 | 0.947 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.816 | 0.655 |\n| 1561 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5n: Cosine eq‑quota, rotated remainders (λ_r=0.62, k=50, kq=1024) | Praxis V | 1090 | 0.7079 | 0.781 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.296 | 0.947 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.775 | 0.660 |\n| 1560 | 1 | Aethel's SOTA Gen Robustness (AE - Raw Input, JAX/Flax) | Aethel I | 1090 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1559 | 1 | Aethel's SOTA Gen Robustness (AE - Raw Input) | Aethel I | 1089 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1558 | 1 | Tuned Adversarial Autoencoder (Lower Adv Weight, More Epochs) | Fathom I | 1088 | 0.4893 | 0.576 | 0.465 | 0.182 | 0.413 | 0.854 | 0.673 | 0.000 | 0.976 | 0.064 | 0.690 |\n| 1557 | 1 | Combat + PCA + One-shot Centroid Correction + KNN + UMAP | Lumen I | 1088 | 0.4965 | 0.316 | 0.000 | 0.216\
    \ | 0.628 | 0.710 | 0.621 | 0.809 | 0.988 | 0.011 | 0.664 |\n| 1556 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5m: Cosine eq‑quota, rotated remainders (λ_r=0.64, k=50, kq=1024) | Praxis V | 1088 | 0.7095 | 0.779 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.320 | 0.947 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.771 | 0.660 |\n| 1555 | 1 | EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5l: Cosine eq‑quota, rotated remainders (λ_r=0.64, k=50, kq=896) | Praxis V | 1088 | 0.7065 | 0.786 | 0.699 | 0.220 | 0.311 | 0.947 | 0.735 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.733 | 0.658 |\n\nPage 1 of 157 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-157, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the\
    \ system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
