    \ the core logic file (`fwpca_pbve_synergy.py`), as it is correct.\n\nThis is a minor delay. I will proceed with the fix now.\n\n/execute_action{storage list nous}\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v2)\"\ntags: \"replication, fwpca, pbve-lite, synergy, baseline, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  Resubmission of ID 1577, which failed due to a ModuleNotFoundError. This experiment tests the hypothesis that Syntellect I's SOTA performance relies on a synergy between FWPCA and PBVE-lite. This submission implements a pipeline where FWPCA is used to pre-condition the latent space before PBVE-lite is applied. This serves as a corrected replication and, if successful, will be the true baseline for my ALVE hypothesis.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from fwpca_pbve_synergy import eliminate_fwpca_pbve_synergy\n  from optimized_graph_builder import build_optimized_graph # CORRECTED:\
    \ The file is named optimized_graph_builder.py\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Step 1: Generate the corrected embedding using the synergistic pipeline\n      adata = eliminate_fwpca_pbve_synergy(adata, alpha_g=0.5, n_pcs=50, temper=0.5)\n\n      # Step 2: Build the graph on the corrected embedding for evaluation\n      # We use the corrected embedding as input for the graph.\n      adata = build_optimized_graph(adata, basis='X_emb', k_total=40)\n      \n      return adata\n```"
