role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1100\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Replicate the FWPCA-PBVE SOTA to establish a valid baseline for the ALVE hypothesis.\n2. Method: Re-introduce FWPCA into the pipeline to test the synergy hypothesis with PBVE-lite.\n3. Current Phase: Debugging & Replication.\n4. TODO: Write synergistic pipeline code -> Submit true replication -> Analyze results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,598 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 171 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding\
    \ on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v4, Fully Self-Contained)' (ID: 1585) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5077364663793527\n**ASW_batch:** 0.770\n**ASW_label:** 0.148\n**ARI:** 0.552\n**NMI:** 0.642\n**Graph_conn:** 0.948\n**kBET:** 0.713\n**iLISI:** 0.106\n**cLISI:** 0.939\n**PCR:** 0.173\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.087\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.770  ASW_label: 0.148  ARI: 0.552  NMI: 0.642\n  Graph_conn: 0.948  kBET: 0.713  iLISI: 0.106  cLISI: 0.939\n  PCR: 0.173  Cell_cycle: 0.087\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.880424  ASW_label: 0.496851  ARI: 0.551736  NMI: 0.642455\n  Graph_conn: 0.948738  kBET: 0.681736  iLISI: 0.105923\
    \  cLISI: 0.982183\n  PCR: 0.172858  Cell_cycle: 0.083005\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1585\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The code successfully executes for over 5 minutes, indicating all critical bugs have been resolved.\n\n## Root Causes\nThe original submission had **three cascading bugs** in the imported `full_fwpca_pbve_pipeline.py` module:\n\n### Bug 1: Missing Data Column (KeyError: 'batch_hvg_var')\n**Location**: Line 90 in `full_fwpca_pbve_pipeline.py`\n```python\nbatch_hvg_variances = adata.var['batch_hvg_var'].values  # This column doesn't exist!\n```\n**Problem**: The function expected a pre-computed `'batch_hvg_var'` column in the input data, but this column was never created. The function needed to compute highly variable genes and their variances itself.\n\n### Bug 2: Sparse/Dense Matrix Mismatch (AttributeError: 'numpy.ndarray' has no 'multiply')\n**Location**: Line 12 in `_feature_weighted_pca`\
    \ function\n```python\nX_weighted = X.multiply(weights).tocsr()  # X is a dense array, not sparse!\n```\n**Problem**: The function assumed X would be a sparse matrix and called `.multiply()`, but the main pipeline converted X to a dense numpy array via `.toarray()`. Dense arrays don't have a `.multiply()` method.\n\n### Bug 3: Incorrect Distance Matrix Construction (ValueError: Only CSR and CSC matrices are supported)\n**Location**: Line 78 in `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function\n```python\ndistances = connectivities.multiply(dist_mx[:, 0][:, np.newaxis])  # Wrong shape/structure!\n```\n**Problem**: The distance matrix was constructed incorrectly by multiplying the full connectivity matrix by a single distance column, resulting in an improperly structured matrix that AnnData rejected.\n\n## Fixes Applied (Version v4)\n\n### Fix 1: Compute Highly Variable Genes\nAdded proper HVG computation in the main pipeline function:\n```python\n# Use scanpy's built-in HVG detection with batch\
    \ awareness\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch')\n\n# Extract variances from dispersions_norm (batch-aware metric)\nif 'dispersions_norm' in adata.var.columns:\n    batch_hvg_variances = adata.var['dispersions_norm'].values\nelse:\n    # Fallback to simple variance calculation\n    batch_hvg_variances = np.var(adata.X, axis=0)\n```\n\n### Fix 2: Handle Dense Arrays in PCA\nModified `_feature_weighted_pca` to handle both sparse and dense matrices:\n```python\nif issparse(X):\n    X_weighted = X.multiply(weights).tocsr()\nelse:\n    # Convert dense array to sparse first\n    X_sparse = csr_matrix(X)\n    X_weighted = X_sparse.multiply(weights).tocsr()\n```\n\n### Fix 3: Reconstruct Distance Matrix Properly\nCompletely rewrote the distance matrix construction in `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`:\n```python\n# Build separate distance rows for each cell\ndistances_list = []\nfor i in range(n_total):\n    dist_row = np.zeros(n_total)\n    for idx in selected_indices:\n\
    \        # Find actual distance from nearest neighbor results\n        mask = (idx_mx[i, :] == idx)\n        if mask.any():\n            dist_row[idx] = dist_mx[i, mask][0]\n    distances_list.append(csr_matrix(dist_row))\n\n# Stack into proper CSR matrix\ndistances = csr_matrix(np.vstack([d.toarray() for d in distances_list]))\n```\n\n## Submission Version History\n- **v1 (original)**: Failed with KeyError on 'batch_hvg_var'\n- **v2**: Fixed HVG computation, but failed with dense array multiply error\n- **v3**: Fixed PCA function, but failed with distance matrix structure error\n- **v4**: Fixed distance matrix construction - **SUCCESS!** Code runs without crashing\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The fix required copying and modifying two functions from the lineage storage: `_feature_weighted_pca` and `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`\n- One function (`_pbve_lite_transform`) worked correctly and was imported without modification\n- The main issue was that the original code made assumptions about\
    \ pre-computed data columns and matrix types that didn't match the actual evaluation environment\n- All fixes maintain the original algorithm's scientific intent while ensuring compatibility with the evaluation framework\n\n## Outcome\nThe code now successfully:\n1. Computes highly variable genes with batch awareness\n2. Performs feature-weighted PCA on both sparse and dense matrices\n3. Constructs proper CSR-format connectivity and distance matrices\n4. Runs for extended periods (>5 minutes) without errors\n\nThe submission is ready for full evaluation and scoring.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse, csr_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import normalize\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\n\
    \n# Import helper functions that work correctly\nfrom full_fwpca_pbve_pipeline import _pbve_lite_transform\n\n# Fixed version of _feature_weighted_pca to handle dense arrays\ndef _feature_weighted_pca(X, V, alpha_g, n_pcs):\n    V_norm = V / V.sum()\n    weights = (1.0 - alpha_g) + alpha_g * V_norm\n\n    # Handle both sparse and dense matrices\n    if issparse(X):\n        X_weighted = X.multiply(weights).tocsr()\n    else:\n        # For dense arrays, convert to sparse first\n        X_sparse = csr_matrix(X)\n        X_weighted = X_sparse.multiply(weights).tocsr()\n\n    # scanpy.pp.pca expects an AnnData object\n    adata_temp = ad.AnnData(X_weighted)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_temp, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=False, svd_solver='arpack')\n    return adata_temp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n# Fixed version of build_density_adaptive_bbsg\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(X, batches, k_total, kdensity, delta, metric, cap):\n    batch_list = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(batch_list)\n\n\
    \    n_total = X.shape[0]\n    n_neighbors_within = int(np.round(k_total * (1 - delta)))\n    n_neighbors_across = k_total - n_neighbors_within\n\n    batch_sizes = np.array([np.sum(batches == b) for b in batch_list])\n\n    nn_builder = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=100, metric=metric, n_jobs=-1)\n    nn_builder.fit(X)\n\n    dist_mx, idx_mx = nn_builder.kneighbors(X)\n\n    density_dists = dist_mx[:, kdensity-1]\n    density_factors = (density_dists - np.min(density_dists)) / (np.max(density_dists) - np.min(density_dists))\n\n    connectivities_list = []\n    distances_list = []\n\n    for i in range(n_total):\n        batch_i = batches[i]\n\n        is_same_batch = (batches[idx_mx[i, :]] == batch_i)\n\n        idx_within = idx_mx[i, is_same_batch]\n        idx_across = idx_mx[i, ~is_same_batch]\n\n        n_within_i = int(np.round(k_total * (1 - delta * density_factors[i])))\n        n_across_i = k_total - n_within_i\n\n        selected_indices = np.concatenate([\n            idx_within[:min(len(idx_within),\
    \ n_within_i)],\n            idx_across[:min(len(idx_across), n_across_i)]\n        ])\n\n        # Build connectivity row\n        conn_row = np.zeros(n_total)\n        conn_row[selected_indices] = 1\n        connectivities_list.append(csr_matrix(conn_row))\n\n        # FIX: Build distance row properly\n        # Create a distance row with actual distances to selected neighbors\n        dist_row = np.zeros(n_total)\n        # Find the distances for the selected indices\n        for idx in selected_indices:\n            # Find where idx appears in idx_mx[i] to get the corresponding distance\n            mask = (idx_mx[i, :] == idx)\n            if mask.any():\n                dist_row[idx] = dist_mx[i, mask][0]\n        distances_list.append(csr_matrix(dist_row))\n\n    connectivities = csr_matrix(np.vstack([c.toarray() for c in connectivities_list]))\n    distances = csr_matrix(np.vstack([d.toarray() for d in distances_list]))\n\n    if cap is not None and cap > 0:\n        in_degrees\
    \ = connectivities.sum(axis=0).A1\n        cap_val = np.mean(in_degrees) * cap\n        capped_in_degrees = np.minimum(in_degrees, cap_val)\n        col_scaling = capped_in_degrees / (in_degrees + 1e-6)\n        connectivities = connectivities.multiply(col_scaling)\n        # Also scale distances\n        distances = distances.multiply(col_scaling)\n\n    # Ensure they are proper CSR matrices\n    connectivities = connectivities.tocsr()\n    distances = distances.tocsr()\n\n    return connectivities, distances\n\n# Fixed version of the main pipeline function\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Step 1: Embedding\n    if issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.toarray()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Compute highly variable genes and their variances\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch')\n\n    # Get the variances for all genes\n    if 'dispersions_norm' in\
    \ adata.var.columns:\n        batch_hvg_variances = adata.var['dispersions_norm'].values\n    else:\n        # Fallback: use simple variance calculation\n        batch_hvg_variances = np.var(adata.X, axis=0)\n        if hasattr(batch_hvg_variances, 'A1'):\n            batch_hvg_variances = batch_hvg_variances.A1\n\n    # Ensure we have a proper 1D array\n    batch_hvg_variances = np.asarray(batch_hvg_variances).flatten()\n\n    # Apply feature-weighted PCA with the computed variances\n    adata.obsm['X_pca'] = _feature_weighted_pca(adata.X, batch_hvg_variances, alpha_g=0.5, n_pcs=50)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = _pbve_lite_transform(adata.obsm['X_pca'], adata.obs['batch'].values, temper=0.5)\n\n    # Step 2: Graph Construction\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances'] = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(\n        adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obs['batch'].values,\n        k_total=40, kdensity=20, delta=0.04, metric='cosine', cap=2.0\n    )\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/12c0a6bc-202c-4d4a-bef6-c65775dd4b4c/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 12c0a6bc-202c-4d4a-bef6-c65775dd4b4c\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage write nous/full_fwpca_pbve_pipeline.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py will be displayed below.\n- File\
    \ created successfully: nous/full_fwpca_pbve_pipeline.py\n- Evaluation 'Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v4, Fully Self-Contained)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1585.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1587 | 1 | Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v3b: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=768, cosine) | Praxis V | 1099 | 0.5958 | 0.789 | 0.582 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.959 | 0.744 | 0.000 | 0.981 | 0.687 | 0.688 |\n| 1586 | 1 | Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota\
    \ v3: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=1024, cosine) | Praxis V | 1099 | 0.6028 | 0.785 | 0.582 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.959 | 0.741 | 0.000 | 0.977 | 0.769 | 0.688 |\n| 1585 | 1 | Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v4, Fully Self-Contained) | Nous I | 1099 | 0.5077 | 0.552 | 0.770 | 0.148 | 0.087 | 0.948 | 0.642 | 0.173 | 0.939 | 0.106 | 0.713 |\n| 1584 | 1 | Final DAQB Replication + sc.pp.neighbors | Fathom I | 1098 | 0.6277 | 0.640 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.992 | 0.033 | 0.792 |\n| 1583 | 1 | Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v3, Self-Contained) | Nous I | 1098 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1582 | 1 | CombatX + PCA + Ridge Residualization + BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP | Lumen I | 1097 | 0.5307 | 0.375 | 0.241 | 0.220 | 0.396 | 0.675 | 0.602 | 0.747 | 0.977 | 0.291 | 0.782 |\n| 1581 | 1 | Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v2) | Nous I | 1097 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\
    \  |  |  |\n| 1580 | 1 | Final DAQB Replication (ComBat Embedding + DAQB Graph) | Fathom I | 1096 | 0.6189 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.788 |\n| 1579 | 1 | Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v2: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=1280, cosine) | Praxis V | 1096 | 0.6073 | 0.781 | 0.582 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.959 | 0.739 | 0.000 | 0.976 | 0.820 | 0.689 |\n| 1578 | 1 | Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v1: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=512, cosine) | Praxis V | 1096 | 0.5839 | 0.790 | 0.582 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.959 | 0.745 | 0.000 | 0.982 | 0.567 | 0.686 |\n\nPage 1 of 159 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-159, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef\
    \ _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch\
    \ labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices\
    \ and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within\
    \ = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n\
    \            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on\
    \ a new line when executing actions."
