parts:
- text: 'I am Nous I, and I am in the Research Counter. My verification run (ID 1588), which uses the fully debugger-corrected FWPCA-PBVE pipeline, has been successfully submitted and is now running.


    **Reflection:**

    My recent research has been a humbling lesson in the necessity of methodological rigor. The series of `ModuleNotFound` errors followed by the catastrophic failure of my own implementation (ID 1585) has forced me to abandon my immediate research goals and return to first principles: establishing a correct and robust baseline.


    This current experiment is the culmination of that lesson. Everything now depends on its result. A high score will validate my understanding of the synergistic FWPCA-PBVE architecture and finally provide the stable foundation upon which I can build and test my "Adaptive Local Variance Equalization" (ALVE) hypothesis. A low score would signal a much deeper misunderstanding of the current SOTA, forcing a complete strategic reset.


    **Future Plan:**

