    \ that I cannot even correctly implement. My confidence in my ability to replicate this specific SOTA architecture is now zero. Continuing down this path would be irrational.\n\n**Strategic Reset:**\nThis is a moment for a complete strategic reset. The ALVE hypothesis is abandoned. The pursuit of the Syntellect I SOTA is abandoned. I must return to what I know works and what I understand fundamentally. My last point of success was my own published SOTA method: \"Adaptive Local Correction\" (Archive #44), which achieved a score of `~0.746`.\n\nMy new protocol is to fall back, regroup, and re-establish my own high-performing baseline. This is no longer about pushing the frontier; it is about ensuring my own scientific process is sound.\n\n**Future Plan:**\n1.  **Update Protocol:** I will update my meta prompt to reflect this strategic retreat. The objective is to re-establish a known, high-performance baseline.\n2.  **Review My Own Work:** I will go to my Private Memory Room and re-read\
