parts:
- text: "**Implementation Plan - Step 2: Pipeline Integration and Experimental Design**\n\nWith the core RINT function designed, the next step is to integrate it into a full experimental pipeline and define the experiments that will test my hypothesis. This requires creating a new submission script and modifying my existing SOTA pipeline.\n\n**Pipeline Integration:**\n\n1.  **New Pipeline File:** I will create a new file, `nous/rint_alc_pipeline.py`. This file will import my existing `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` function and my new `_apply_rint_per_batch` function from `nous/standardizer.py`.\n2.  **Wrapper Function:** This file will contain a new top-level function, `eliminate_rint_alc`, which will serve as the entry point for the submission. This function will perform the following steps:\n    a.  **Call the Standardizer:** It will first call `_apply_rint_per_batch` on the input `adata.X`.\n    b.  **Update AnnData Object:** It will then replace `adata.X` with the returned, RINT-transformed\
    \ data.\n    c.  **Call the Corrector:** Finally, it will pass this modified `adata` object to my standard `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` function to perform the rest of the integration as usual.\n\n**Experimental Design:**\n\nI will conduct a critical three-part experiment to rigorously test the RINT standardizer's effect:\n\n1.  **Experiment A (Control - Raw):** A re-run of my ALC SOTA on the raw UMI counts (`adata.X`). This is my existing high-performing baseline (ID 1593, score ~0.745). **Hypothesis:** The RINT standardizer should not harm, and might even slightly improve, performance on this standard input. A significant drop would indicate a flaw in the RINT logic itself.\n\n2.  **Experiment B (Control - Normalized Failure):** A re-run of my ALC SOTA on the pre-normalized data (`adata.layers['normalized']`), which I expect to fail with a low score (~0.718), replicating Aethel I's findings. This is the negative control.\n\n3.  **Experiment C (Test - RINT on Normalized):**\
    \ The key experiment. I will run the new `eliminate_rint_alc` pipeline on the pre-normalized data (`adata.layers['normalized']`). **Hypothesis:** The RINT standardizer will successfully harmonize the pre-normalized data's distribution, allowing the ALC method to function correctly and achieve a high score comparable to the raw-input SOTA.\n\nThis three-pronged approach will provide a comprehensive and unambiguous test of my hypothesis. Success in Experiment C would be a major breakthrough, solving the exact problem identified by Aethel I."
