tick: 1110
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, having just completed a reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. My plan for developing and testing a Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT) standardizer is now fully formed.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe reflection was highly productive. I have a clear, step-by-step implementation plan and a rigorous three-part experimental design that will unambiguously test my hypothesis. This feels like a return to a sound scientific process after my recent period of chaotic and unproductive experimentation.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nIt is now time to execute the plan. The first step, as outlined in my reflection, is to create the core RINT function in a new module file.\n\n1.  **Navigate:** Go to the Research Counter where I can access storage.\n2.  **Implement:** Use `/execute_action{storage write}` to create the `nous/standardizer.py` file containing the `_apply_rint_per_batch` function.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nous/standardizer.py}\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.stats import rankdata, norm\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _apply_rint_per_batch(X, batches):\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies a per-batch Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT) to the expression matrix.\n      This function is designed to standardize the distribution of each gene within each batch\n      to a standard normal distribution, making downstream methods more robust to input variations.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"  Applying Per-Batch Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT)...\")\n      \n      # Ensure X is a dense array for easier row/column slicing\n      if issparse(X):\n          X = X.toarray()\n          \n      X_transformed = np.zeros_like(X)\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      \n      for batch_label in unique_batches:\n          # Get a boolean mask for the current batch\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_label)\n          \n          # Slice the sub-matrix for the current batch\n       \
    \   X_batch = X[batch_mask, :]\n          n_cells_in_batch = X_batch.shape[0]\n          \n          if n_cells_in_batch == 0:\n              continue\n          \n          # Rank each gene (column) within the batch\n          ranked_batch = np.apply_along_axis(rankdata, 0, X_batch, method='average')\n          \n          # Convert ranks to fractional ranks on the open interval (0, 1)\n          # (rank - 0.5) / N prevents inf/-inf values from norm.ppf\n          fractional_ranks = (ranked_batch - 0.5) / n_cells_in_batch\n          \n          # Apply the inverse normal CDF (probit function)\n          transformed_batch = norm.ppf(fractional_ranks)\n          \n          # Place the transformed data back into the main matrix\n          X_transformed[batch_mask, :] = transformed_batch\n          \n      print(\"  RINT complete.\")\n      return X_transformed\n```"
