tick: 1111
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. I have successfully created the `standardizer.py` file containing my core RINT logic.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe first implementation step is complete. Now I must create the pipeline that integrates this new module with my existing ALC method. As per my reflection, this involves creating a new file that imports both the standardizer and the ALC functions and combines them into a single, cohesive workflow.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nI will now execute Step 2 of my implementation plan: creating the integrated pipeline file. After this, I will be ready to begin the three-part experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nous/rint_alc_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n\n  # Import the two core components of the new pipeline\n  from standardizer import _apply_rint_per_batch\n  from local_adaptive_correction import eliminate_local_adaptive_correction\n\n  def eliminate_rint_alc(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData, input_layer=None) -> ad.Annata:\n      \"\"\"\n      A novel pipeline that first applies a Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT)\n      to standardize the input data, then applies the Adaptive Local Correction (ALC) method.\n      \n      Args:\n          adata: The AnnData object.\n          input_layer: Specifies which data to use. If None, uses adata.X.\n                       If 'normalized', uses adata.layers['normalized'].\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"[Nous I] Executing RINT+ALC pipeline.\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Select the input data\n      if input_layer == 'normalized':\n          print(\"  Using pre-normalized data from adata.layers['normalized'].\")\n          input_data = adata.layers['normalized']\n      else:\n          print(\"  Using standard data from adata.X.\")\n          input_data = adata.X\n      \n      # Step 2: Apply the RINT Standardizer\n      # The standardizer returns a transformed numpy array.\n      rint_transformed_data = _apply_rint_per_batch(input_data,\
    \ adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      \n      # Create a new AnnData object for the correction step, as ALC expects it.\n      # It's safer to create a new object than to modify the input in place.\n      adata_for_correction = ad.AnnData(X=rint_transformed_data, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.copy())\n      \n      # Step 3: Apply the Adaptive Local Correction method\n      # The ALC function will handle its own internal preprocessing (log1p, HVG, etc.)\n      # on the now-standardized data.\n      print(\"  Passing standardized data to Adaptive Local Correction method.\")\n      adata_corrected = eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata_for_correction, delta=0.04)\n      \n      return adata_corrected\n```"
