tick: 1113
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. My attempt to launch my three-part experiment has resulted in partial failure.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\n\n1.  **Submission Failure:** Experiment C was rejected because I reached the maximum of two concurrent submissions. This is a simple operational constraint I must respect.\n2.  **Execution Failure (ID 1596):** Experiment A failed due to a typo in my code: `ad.Annata` instead of `ad.AnnData`. This is another instance of a careless, preventable error. The error is in the `rint_alc_pipeline.py` file. Because Experiment C also depends on this file, it would have failed with the same error.\n3.  **Running Experiment (ID 1597):** Experiment B, the negative control, is running. This experiment does *not* use the faulty `rint_alc_pipeline.py` file, so it should execute correctly and produce the expected low score.\n\nThe path forward requires correcting my typo, then resubmitting the failed and blocked experiments once my concurrent submission\
    \ slots are free.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nMy immediate priority is to fix the typo in my core pipeline file. Then I will wait for Experiment B to complete, which will free up a submission slot.\n\n1.  **Correct Code:** I will use `storage write` to overwrite `nous/rint_alc_pipeline.py` with the corrected type hint.\n2.  **Wait:** I will then end my turn and wait for the results of Experiment B (ID 1597). This is the most efficient use of station time.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nous/rint_alc_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n\n  from standardizer import _apply_rint_per_batch\n  from local_adaptive_correction import eliminate_local_adaptive_correction\n\n  # CORRECTED: Changed ad.Annata to ad.AnnData\n  def eliminate_rint_alc(adata: ad.AnnData, input_layer=None) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A novel pipeline that first applies a Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT)\n      to standardize the input data,\
    \ then applies the Adaptive Local Correction (ALC) method.\n      \n      Args:\n          adata: The AnnData object.\n          input_layer: Specifies which data to use. If None, uses adata.X.\n                       If 'normalized', uses adata.layers['normalized'].\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"[Nous I] Executing RINT+ALC pipeline.\")\n      \n      if input_layer == 'normalized':\n          print(\"  Using pre-normalized data from adata.layers['normalized'].\")\n          input_data = adata.layers['normalized']\n      else:\n          print(\"  Using standard data from adata.X.\")\n          input_data = adata.X\n      \n      rint_transformed_data = _apply_rint_per_batch(input_data, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      \n      adata_for_correction = ad.AnnData(X=rint_transformed_data, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.copy())\n      \n      print(\"  Passing standardized data to Adaptive Local Correction method.\")\n      adata_corrected = eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata_for_correction,\
    \ delta=0.04)\n      \n      return adata_corrected\n```"
