parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. The results for Experiment B are in, and I have corrected the typo in my RINT pipeline.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\n\n*   **Experiment B Result (ID 1597):** Score = `0.7195`. This is a success. It perfectly replicates the failure mode identified by Aethel I, confirming that my ALC method does not generalize to pre-normalized data. The negative control is established.\n\n*   **Typo Fix:** I have corrected the `ad.Annata` typo in `rint_alc_pipeline.py`. The code for Experiments A and C is now ready for execution.\n\n*   **Current State:** I now have one free submission slot.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nMy experimental plan is back on track. I will now resubmit Experiment A (the positive control) and Experiment C (the primary hypothesis test).\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"RINT Experiment A: RINT + ALC on Raw Counts (v2)\"\ntags: \"rint, standardizer, control-experiment, adaptive-local-correction, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  Resubmission\
    \ of ID 1596, which failed due to a typo. Part A of a three-part experiment testing a new Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT) standardizer. This experiment applies the RINT preprocessor to the standard raw UMI counts before passing them to my SOTA ALC pipeline. This is a positive control to test if RINT is harmful to a high-performing baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from rint_alc_pipeline import eliminate_rint_alc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_rint_alc(adata, input_layer=None)\n```\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"RINT Experiment C: RINT + ALC on Normalized Data (Hypothesis Test, v2)\"\ntags: \"rint, standardizer, novel-hypothesis, adaptive-local-correction, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  Resubmission of the blocked Experiment C. This is the primary test of my new hypothesis. This experiment applies the Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT) standardizer\
    \ to the pre-normalized data (`adata.layers['normalized']`) before passing it to my ALC pipeline. The hypothesis is that RINT will fix the data distribution issues and rescue performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from rint_alc_pipeline import eliminate_rint_alc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_rint_alc(adata, input_layer='normalized')\n```"
