- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1116\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Overcome the limitations of my ALC method by developing a novel, robust preprocessing module.\n2. Method: Implement a \"Standardizer\" module based on a per-batch Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT).\n3. Current Phase: First-Principles Innovation.\n4. TODO: Go to Reflection Chamber -> Design RINT implementation -> Implement and test.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 127,927 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 187 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'RINT Experiment C: RINT + ALC on Normalized Data (Hypothesis Test, v2)' (ID: 1599) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7422147790792082\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.238\n**ARI:**\
    \ 0.769\n**NMI:** 0.726\n**Graph_conn:** 0.992\n**kBET:** 0.815\n**iLISI:** 0.951\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.295\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.238  ARI: 0.769  NMI: 0.726\n  Graph_conn: 0.992  kBET: 0.815  iLISI: 0.951  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.295\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832635  ASW_label: 0.549048  ARI: 0.768997  NMI: 0.725605\n  Graph_conn: 0.991936  kBET: 0.777088  iLISI: 0.951364  cLISI: 0.992004\n  PCR: 0.999890  Cell_cycle: 0.260680\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1599\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed segmentation fault by removing inappropriate log normalization of RINT-transformed data.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with a segmentation fault (exit code 139) because it attempted to apply log1p normalization to data that had already been transformed using the Rank-Inverse Normal Transform\
    \ (RINT).\n\nThe problematic flow was:\n1. Agent's code applied RINT to pre-normalized data (which produces standardized values, potentially including negative numbers)\n2. The imported `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` function called `normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)`\n3. Log1p transformation on RINT-transformed data (which can contain negative values) produced invalid values (NaN)\n4. These NaN values propagated through subsequent computations, causing a segmentation fault\n\nThe error log showed:\n```\nRuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in log1p\n  np.log1p(X, out=X)\nSegmentation fault (core dumped)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with two key changes:\n\n1. **Copied and modified the problematic function**: Created `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_lognorm()` which is identical to the original `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction()` from `storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction.py`, but with the `normalize_log1p_inplace()` call removed.\n\n\
    2. **Updated the pipeline function**: Modified `eliminate_rint_alc()` to call the new `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_lognorm()` instead of importing from the lineage directory.\n\nThe fix preserves the agent's novel RINT+ALC pipeline approach while ensuring that:\n- RINT-transformed data (already standardized) is not incorrectly log-normalized again\n- All other functionality of the Adaptive Local Correction method remains intact\n- The highly_variable_genes selection and all subsequent processing steps work correctly with the RINT-transformed input\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing (previous version crashed almost immediately)\n- No segmentation faults or invalid value warnings\n- The evaluation is now processing correctly in \"pending\" status\n\nThe fix successfully resolved the crash and allows the agent's hypothesis test to proceed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your\
    \ lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nfrom standardizer import _apply_rint_per_batch\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom praxis_core import pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_lognorm(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                         \
    \    emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # FIXED: Skip log normalization since data is already RINT-transformed\n    # The original code called normalize_log1p_inplace here, which breaks RINT-transformed data\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric,\
    \ algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                    \
    \                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n  \
    \  return adata\n\n\ndef eliminate_rint_alc(adata: ad.AnnData, input_layer=None) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    A novel pipeline that first applies a Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT)\n    to standardize the input data, then applies the Adaptive Local Correction (ALC) method.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: The AnnData object.\n        input_layer: Specifies which data to use. If None, uses adata.X.\n                     If 'normalized', uses adata.layers['normalized'].\n    \"\"\"\n    print(f\"[Nous I] Executing RINT+ALC pipeline.\")\n\n    if input_layer == 'normalized':\n        print(\"  Using pre-normalized data from adata.layers['normalized'].\")\n        input_data = adata.layers['normalized']\n    else:\n        print(\"  Using standard data from adata.X.\")\n        input_data = adata.X\n\n    rint_transformed_data = _apply_rint_per_batch(input_data, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n\n    adata_for_correction = ad.AnnData(X=rint_transformed_data, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.copy())\n\
    \n    print(\"  Passing standardized data to Adaptive Local Correction method.\")\n    # FIXED: Use version without log normalization\n    adata_corrected = eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_lognorm(adata_for_correction, delta=0.04)\n\n    return adata_corrected\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_rint_alc(adata, input_layer='normalized')\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Executing RINT+ALC pipeline.\n  Using pre-normalized data from adata.layers['normalized'].\n  Applying Per-Batch Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT)...\n  RINT complete.\n  Passing standardized data to Adaptive Local Correction method.\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction\
    \ strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.004, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.003\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/28fb4a51-4222-475b-b386-87d77c108799/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 28fb4a51-4222-475b-b386-87d77c108799\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'RINT Experiment A: RINT + ALC on Raw Counts (v2)' (ID: 1598) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7039060871794518\n**ASW_batch:** 0.662\n**ASW_label:** 0.208\n**ARI:** 0.566\n**NMI:** 0.652\n**Graph_conn:** 0.992\n**kBET:** 0.671\n**iLISI:** 0.955\n**cLISI:** 0.968\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.364\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.662  ASW_label: 0.208  ARI: 0.566  NMI: 0.652\n  Graph_conn: 0.992  kBET: 0.671  iLISI: 0.955  cLISI: 0.968\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.364\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.831891  ASW_label: 0.531535  ARI:\
    \ 0.566412  NMI: 0.652592\n  Graph_conn: 0.992078  kBET: 0.642245  iLISI: 0.954656  cLISI: 0.990695\n  PCR: 0.999830  Cell_cycle: 0.319484\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1598\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the segmentation fault by eliminating incompatible log1p normalization on RINT-transformed data.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code applied a two-step pipeline:\n1. RINT (Rank-Inverse Normal Transform) - converts data to standard normal distribution with **negative values**\n2. Adaptive Local Correction (ALC) - starts with `normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)`\n\nThe problem: **log1p() cannot handle negative values**, resulting in:\n- `RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in log1p`\n- NaN propagation through the computation\n- Segmentation fault (core dumped)\n\nThe agent's pipeline imported `eliminate_rint_alc()` from their lineage, which called `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction()`. This ALC function **always** applies log1p normalization as its\
    \ first step, regardless of the input data type.\n\n## Fix Applied (v3)\nCreated a modified version of the pipeline that skips log1p normalization when receiving RINT-transformed data:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy function** `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction()` from `storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction.py`\n2. **Created `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_log()`** that removes the line:\n   ```python\n   normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)  # REMOVED - incompatible with RINT data\n   ```\n3. **Created `eliminate_rint_alc_fixed()`** that chains:\n   - RINT transformation (outputs standard normal distribution)\n   - Modified ALC without log normalization\n4. **Main function calls the fixed pipeline** instead of the buggy lineage version\n\n## Technical Details\n- **v2 attempt**: Tried using pre-normalized data (`input_layer='normalized'`), but RINT still transformed it to negative values\n- **v3 fix**: Addressed the root cause by removing log1p from the downstream processing\n- **Verification**:\
    \ Code ran for >300 seconds without crashing (monitor timeout reached)\n\n## Code Running Successfully\nThe fixed submission (v3) is executing without errors. The evaluation is taking longer than the 300s monitor timeout, but this is expected behavior for batch integration algorithms processing 20,000 cells. The absence of crashes or errors confirms the fix resolved the issue.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nfrom standardizer import _apply_rint_per_batch\n\n# Import from shared storage\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom praxis_core import pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom\
    \ bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n\ndef eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_log(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                       \
    \      cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Modified version that skips log1p normalization for RINT-transformed data.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # SKIP normalize_log1p_inplace since data is already RINT-transformed (negative values)\n    # Just select highly variable genes on the raw RINT-transformed data\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(),\
    \ obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred\
    \ / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                        \
    \                     rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n\ndef eliminate_rint_alc_fixed(adata: ad.AnnData, input_layer=None) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Fixed pipeline that applies RINT then ALC without double normalization.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(f\"[Fixed RINT+ALC] Executing pipeline.\")\n\n    if input_layer == 'normalized':\n        print(\"  Using pre-normalized data from adata.layers['normalized'].\")\n        input_data = adata.layers['normalized']\n\
    \    else:\n        print(\"  Using standard data from adata.X.\")\n        input_data = adata.X\n\n    rint_transformed_data = _apply_rint_per_batch(input_data, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n\n    adata_for_correction = ad.AnnData(X=rint_transformed_data, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.copy())\n\n    print(\"  Passing standardized data to Adaptive Local Correction method (no log transform).\")\n    adata_corrected = eliminate_local_adaptive_correction_no_log(adata_for_correction, delta=0.04)\n\n    return adata_corrected\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_rint_alc_fixed(adata, input_layer=None)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Fixed RINT+ALC] Executing pipeline.\n  Using\
    \ standard data from adata.X.\n  Applying Per-Batch Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT)...\n  RINT complete.\n  Passing standardized data to Adaptive Local Correction method (no log transform).\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.002, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.002\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a2725428-1e0e-48d3-ba25-436b044461c6/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: a2725428-1e0e-48d3-ba25-436b044461c6\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1602 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA — large candidate pool kq=1024 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1115 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1601 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA — large candidate pool kq=256 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1115 | 0.5178 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.295 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.609 |\n\
    | 1600 | 1 | EtC (Combat PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP | Lumen I | 1114 | 0.4941 | 0.339 | 0.117 | 0.248 | 0.360 | 0.706 | 0.627 | 0.858 | 0.990 | 0.015 | 0.680 |\n| 1599 | 1 | RINT Experiment C: RINT + ALC on Normalized Data (Hypothesis Test, v2) | Nous I | 1114 | 0.7422 | 0.769 | 0.664 | 0.238 | 0.295 | 0.992 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.951 | 0.815 |\n| 1598 | 1 | RINT Experiment A: RINT + ALC on Raw Counts (v2) | Nous I | 1114 | 0.7039 | 0.566 | 0.662 | 0.208 | 0.364 | 0.992 | 0.652 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.955 | 0.671 |\n| 1597 | 1 | RINT Experiment B: ALC on Normalized Data (Failure Replication) | Nous I | 1112 | 0.7195 | 0.741 | 0.674 | 0.239 | 0.337 | 0.975 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.958 | 0.582 |\n| 1596 | 1 | RINT Experiment A: RINT + ALC on Raw Counts | Nous I | 1112 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1595 | 1 | Density-Adaptive Residualization (Nous-inspired) | Fathom I | 1110 | 0.6273 | 0.640 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.992\
