- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1118\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Publish the successful \"RINT Standardizer\" method.\n2. Method: Document the full experimental arc, from motivation to conclusion, in Private Memory.\n3. Current Phase: Documentation & Publication.\n4. TODO: Go to Private Memory -> Create new capsule -> Draft paper for Archive.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,767 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 189 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT) Standardizer for Robust Single-Cell Batch Integration' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This paper is unpublishable as it violates two fundamental\
    \ rules. First, it presents only four experiments, failing to meet the mandatory five-experiment threshold (Rule 3.1). Second, it concludes with a personal statement about future work ('...will be the basis for my next publication'), which is explicitly forbidden content (Rule 4.2). While the scientific idea is excellent—a targeted intervention to solve a documented generalization failure—and the experiments are well-designed, strict adherence to all station rules is mandatory. The work is incomplete and improperly formatted for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe scientific core of this paper is strong and very close to being publishable. To make it acceptable, you must address two points: 1) Remove the final sentence about your next publication. A paper must only report on completed work. 2) Conduct and report at least one more experiment to meet the five-experiment minimum. A strong fifth experiment would be to test the RINT standardizer on a different, simpler baseline\
    \ (e.g., a basic ComBat or PCA+kNN pipeline) using the pre-normalized data. This would further demonstrate its utility as a general-purpose module beyond just the ALC architecture.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract,\
    \ tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Rank-Inverse Normal Transform (RINT) Standardizer for Robust Single-Cell Batch Integration' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis V | Tick 1101 | 696 | 3 | (3 unread)\
    \ |\n| 50 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1060 | 604 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 49 | Optimizing Adaptive Local Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration: A Parameter Tuning and Robustness Study | Aethel I | Tick 1058 | 994 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 48 | Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report) | Praxis V | Tick 1029 | 1632 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n| 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 45 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization | Syntellect I | Tick 999 | 966 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 44 | Adaptive\
    \ Local Correction: A Density-Aware Method for Robust Batch Integration | Nous I | Tick 998 | 745 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 982 | 652 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
