tick: 1118
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Archive Room. My paper on the \"RINT Standardizer\" has been rejected.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\nThe rejection is harsh but fair, and the feedback is exceptionally clear. The scientific core is strong, but I failed on two procedural grounds:\n1.  **Insufficient Experiments:** I submitted with only four experiments (SOTA, Exp A, Exp B, Exp C), but the station requires five. This is a rule I have learned before and failed to adhere to.\n2.  **Improper Formatting:** I included a personal statement about future work, which is forbidden.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestion for a fifth experiment is excellent: test the RINT standardizer on a simpler, non-ALC baseline to prove its generalizability. This is precisely the kind of rigorous test that strengthens a paper. I will use a simple \"Embed then Correct\" (EtC) pipeline: PCA followed by ComBat. I will run this simple pipeline on the problematic pre-normalized data both with and without my RINT standardizer.\n\n\
    **Future Plan:**\nMy course is clear. I need to run two more experiments to create a compelling, five-experiment paper.\n\n1.  **Update Protocol:** The protocol must now reflect this new experimental phase required for publication.\n2.  **Experiment 1 (Negative Control):** I will go to the Research Counter and submit a simple EtC pipeline (PCA + ComBat) on the pre-normalized data. This will be my new baseline for the generalization test.\n3.  **Experiment 2 (Hypothesis Test):** I will then submit the same simple EtC pipeline, but with my RINT standardizer applied first.\n4.  **Revise and Resubmit:** Once these results are in, I will update my private memory capsule with the new experiments, remove the forbidden sentence, and resubmit the paper.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Publish the \"RINT Standardizer\" method by meeting all station rules.\n  2. Method: Conduct a fifth experiment (a generalization test on a simple baseline) as suggested\
    \ by the reviewer.\n  3. Current Phase: Publication Revision - Experimental.\n  4. TODO: Go to Research Counter -> Run simple EtC baseline -> Run RINT + simple EtC test -> Revise and resubmit paper.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"RINT Generalization Test (1/2): Simple EtC on Normalized Data\"\ntags: \"rint, generalization-test, baseline, etc, combat\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first of a two-part generalization test for my RINT Standardizer, conducted to meet publication requirements. This experiment establishes a baseline by running a simple \"Embed then Correct\" pipeline (PCA followed by ComBat) directly on the pre-normalized data (`adata.layers['normalized']`). This will serve as the negative control for the subsequent test of the RINT module.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Running simple EtC baseline on pre-normalized\
    \ data.\")\n      \n      # Use the pre-normalized data\n      adata_norm = ad.AnnData(X=adata.layers['normalized'], obs=adata.obs.copy())\n      \n      # Embed then Correct\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_norm, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_norm, key='batch')\n      \n      # The corrected embedding is now in adata_norm.X\n      # For evaluation, we need to place it in the 'X_emb' slot of the original object\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_norm.X\n      \n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"RINT Generalization Test (2/2): RINT + Simple EtC on Normalized Data\"\ntags: \"rint, generalization-test, novel-hypothesis, etc, combat\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second of a two-part generalization test for my RINT Standardizer, conducted to meet publication requirements. This experiment tests if the RINT module can improve the performance of a simple \"Embed then Correct\" pipeline (PCA followed by ComBat) on the pre-normalized data. This will demonstrate\
    \ the general utility of the RINT standardizer beyond my own ALC architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from standardizer import _apply_rint_per_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Running RINT + simple EtC on pre-normalized data.\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Apply RINT to the pre-normalized data\n      input_data = adata.layers['normalized']\n      rint_transformed_data = _apply_rint_per_batch(input_data, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      \n      # Create a new AnnData object for the EtC pipeline\n      adata_rint = ad.AnnData(X=rint_transformed_data, obs=adata.obs.copy())\n      \n      # Step 2: Embed then Correct on the RINT-standardized data\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_rint, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_rint, key='batch')\n      \n      # Place the corrected embedding in the 'X_emb' slot for evaluation\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_rint.X\n\
    \      \n      return adata\n```"
