tick: 1122
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nous I, in the Reflection Chamber. I have just completed an extensive reflection session, designing a novel \"Gene Meta-Correction\" paradigm from first principles.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe planning is complete. I have a clear, step-by-step implementation plan for a high-risk, high-reward hypothesis that breaks from the station's dominant \"Embed then Correct\" paradigm. I have also considered the potential failure modes and have a contingency plan for each outcome. It is now time to translate this plan into action.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nMy protocol needs to be updated to reflect this new experimental phase. Then, I will proceed to the Research Counter to implement and submit my first experiment.\n\n1.  **Update Protocol:** Shift from brainstorming to execution of the \"Gene Meta-Correction\" hypothesis.\n2.  **Navigate:** Go to the Research Counter.\n3.  **Implement and Submit:** Create the self-contained pipeline file `nous/gene_meta_correction.py` and immediately submit the\
    \ first proof-of-concept experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Test the novel \"Gene Meta-Correction\" paradigm.\n  2. Method: Implement and run a proof-of-concept experiment.\n  3. Current Phase: First-Principles Innovation - Execution.\n  4. TODO: Implement pipeline -> Submit experiment -> Analyze.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nous/gene_meta_correction.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _create_gene_meta_features(X, batches, var_names):\n      \"\"\"Creates a meta-feature matrix of gene statistics per batch.\"\"\"\n      print(\"  Creating gene meta-feature space...\")\n      if issparse(X):\n          X = X.toarray()\n      \n      df = pd.DataFrame(X, columns=var_names)\n      df['batch'] = batches\n      \n      # Calculate mean and variance per gene for each\
    \ batch\n      mean_df = df.groupby('batch').mean().transpose() # n_genes x n_batches\n      var_df = df.groupby('batch').var().transpose()   # n_genes x n_batches\n      \n      # Concatenate to form the meta-feature matrix\n      meta_features = pd.concat([mean_df, var_df], axis=1).fillna(0)\n      print(f\"  Meta-feature matrix created with shape: {meta_features.shape}\")\n      return meta_features.values\n\n  def eliminate_gene_meta_correction(adata: ad.AnnData, n_meta_pcs=4) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A novel pipeline that corrects a meta-feature space of genes to create a\n      batch-invariant embedding.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[Nous I] Executing novel 'Gene Meta-Correction' pipeline.\")\n      \n      # 1. Standard Preprocessing\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      \n      adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n\
    \      \n      # 2. Create Gene Meta-Feature Space\n      meta_features = _create_gene_meta_features(adata_hvg.X, adata_hvg.obs['batch'].values, adata_hvg.var_names)\n      \n      # 3. Correct Meta-Features via PCA to get Gene Weights\n      print(f\"  Applying PCA to meta-features to get {n_meta_pcs} gene weights...\")\n      gene_weights = sc.tl.pca(meta_features, n_comps=n_meta_pcs, use_highly_variable=False)\n      \n      # 4. Transform Cell Data using Gene Weights\n      print(\"  Projecting cell data onto learned gene weights...\")\n      X_hvg = adata_hvg.X.toarray() if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n      final_embedding = X_hvg @ gene_weights\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = final_embedding\n      \n      # 5. Build a simple graph for evaluation\n      print(\"  Building kNN graph on final embedding.\")\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15)\n      \n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel Paradigm: Gene Meta-Correction\
    \ (Proof of Concept)\"\ntags: \"novel-hypothesis, first-principles, gene-centric, meta-features\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a new, first-principles paradigm for batch integration called \"Gene Meta-Correction.\" Instead of correcting cells in a biased PCA space, this method first creates a meta-feature space of per-batch gene statistics (e.g., mean, variance). It then applies PCA to this meta-space to learn a set of \"batch-invariant\" gene weights. The original expression data is then projected onto these learned weights to create the final embedding. This is a high-risk proof-of-concept for a new \"correct-the-genes-then-embed\" approach.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from gene_meta_correction import eliminate_gene_meta_correction\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_gene_meta_correction(adata, n_meta_pcs=4)\n```"
