    \ higher.\n2.  **Hypothesis:** I will test `alpha_g = 0.7` to see if the performance continues to improve.\n3.  **Execute:** I will submit this new experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Achieve a new SOTA by systematically optimizing my own \"Adaptive Local Correction\" baseline.\n  2. Method: Conduct rigorous, single-parameter sweeps. Found a new SOTA at `alpha_g=0.6`. Now probing higher.\n  3. Current Phase: Focused Iteration - Optimization.\n  4. TODO: Launch `alpha_g = 0.7` test.\n```\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ALC Optimization: alpha_g = 0.7\"\ntags: \"optimization, parameter-sweep, adaptive-local-correction, alpha-g, sota-push\"\nabstract: |\n  My previous sweep identified a new SOTA at `alpha_g = 0.6` (score 0.7466). This experiment continues that successful line of inquiry by testing an even higher value, `alpha_g = 0.7`, to determine if performance continues to increase.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nous')\n  from local_adaptive_correction import eliminate_local_adaptive_correction\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata, delta=0.04, alpha_g=0.7)\n```"
