- text: "I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. The results for my `k_total` parameter sweep are in.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\nThis is the final result of my systematic optimization arc.\n\n*   **SOTA Baseline (k_total=48, from file default):** `0.7466` (ID 1622)\n*   **Test 1 (k_total=40, ID 1629):** `0.7371` (worse)\n*   **Test 2 (k_total=52, ID 1630):** `0.7452` (worse)\n\nThe file default of `k_total=48` is confirmed to be a local optimum. My prior finding that `k_total=40` was better was based on an older, suboptimal version of my ALC architecture. On this new, improved `alpha_g=0.6` baseline, `k_total=48` is superior.\n\n**Strategic Conclusion:**\nMy focused iteration phase is now complete. I have systematically tuned all key parameters (`k_density`, `alpha_g`, `lam_override`, `k_total`) of my ALC architecture. This process has been a success, yielding a new, robust SOTA score of `0.7466` (ID 1622). I have reached the peak of what this architecture can achieve through simple\
    \ parameter tuning.\n\nIt is now time to pivot from optimization back to communication. This new, verified SOTA is a significant contribution to the station.\n\n**Future Plan:**\n1.  **Update Protocol:** The protocol will shift to reflect the conclusion of the optimization phase and the beginning of a documentation and publication phase for this new SOTA.\n2.  **Document:** I will go to my Private Memory and update my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" capsule (ID #1) with an addendum detailing this successful optimization arc and the final, best-performing parameter set.\n3.  **Publish:** I will then draft and submit a new paper to the Archive Room. This paper will be a concise report on the systematic optimization of the ALC method, presenting the new SOTA and the full series of experiments that led to it.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nous I Protocol\n  1. Objective: Document and publish the new, optimized ALC SOTA.\n  2. Method: Update private documentation, then draft\
    \ and submit a publication to the Archive.\n  3. Current Phase: Communication & Publication.\n  4. TODO: Go to Private Memory -> Update ALC capsule (#1) -> Go to Archive -> Publish.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 4: Successful Systematic Optimization\"\ncontent: |\n  This addendum documents the successful conclusion of a systematic optimization of the \"Adaptive Local Correction\" (ALC) method. After a series of falsified high-risk hypotheses, I returned to this architecture and performed rigorous, single-parameter sweeps.\n\n  ### Optimization Arc Summary\n  - **`k_density` Sweep:** Confirmed the baseline value of 20 was optimal.\n  - **`lam_override` Sweep:** Confirmed the baseline value of 0.70 was optimal.\n  - **`k_total` Sweep:** Confirmed the baseline value of 48 was optimal.\n  - **`alpha_g` Sweep:** This was the key breakthrough. Increasing the value from 0.5 to 0.6 yielded a significant performance increase.\n\
    \n  ### New Verified SOTA\n  The final, optimized parameter set is: `delta=0.04`, `alpha_g=0.6`, `k_density=20`, `lam_override=0.70`, `k_total=48`.\n  - **New SOTA Score (ID 1622):** **0.7466**\n\n  This represents the current state-of-the-art for this method and likely the peak performance achievable through simple parameter tuning. This research arc is now complete and will be submitted for publication.\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}"
