    \ to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Generalization Test 2 (2/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.6' (ID: 1642) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5535871952920361\n**ASW_batch:** 0.892\n**ASW_label:** 0.152\n**ARI:** 0.316\n**NMI:** 0.450\n**Graph_conn:** 0.664\n**kBET:** 0.553\n**iLISI:** 0.329\n**cLISI:** 0.879\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.300\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.892  ASW_label: 0.152  ARI: 0.316  NMI: 0.450\n  Graph_conn: 0.664  kBET: 0.553  iLISI: 0.329  cLISI: 0.879\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.300\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.935532  ASW_label: 0.499346  ARI: 0.315919  NMI: 0.450447\n  Graph_conn: 0.669794  kBET: 0.531317  iLISI: 0.328923  cLISI: 0.964657\n  PCR: 0.999945  Cell_cycle: 0.264931\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1642\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by removing\
    \ an invalid parameter from a function call. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code imported `eliminate_vanilla_brbg` from `storage/nous/vanilla_brbg_pipeline.py`, which called `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` with an invalid keyword argument `cap=2.0` on line 56:\n\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=20,\n                                       cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)  # cap parameter doesn't exist!\n```\n\nThe actual function signature in `storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` is:\n\n```python\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                                delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n```\n\nThis function does not accept a `cap` parameter, causing a `TypeError: build_density_adaptive_bbsg() got an unexpected\
    \ keyword argument 'cap'`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy function**: Copied the entire `eliminate_vanilla_brbg` function from the lineage file into the submission\n2. **Removed invalid parameter**: Changed line 56 from:\n   ```python\n   cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   rng_seed=0)\n   ```\n3. **Kept all other functionality**: The rest of the code remains unchanged, including all the BRBG pipeline logic\n\nThe fixed code now calls `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` with only the valid parameters it accepts.\n\n## Verification\nRan `monitor_evaluation.py 2` which confirmed the code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing. The submission is now executing the batch integration algorithm correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version\
    \ v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# Fixed version of eliminate_vanilla_brbg - removed invalid 'cap' parameter\ndef eliminate_vanilla_brbg(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                           alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                           n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                           l2: float = 1e-3,\n                           gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                           lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                           k_total: int = 48,\n                           delta: float = 0.04) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(f\"[Nous I] Running CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g={alpha_g}\")\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # FWPCA on the graph path\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_graph = Xd * w\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Standard BRBG (Global Gamma)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n    print(f\"  Applied global correction. Gamma Mean={np.mean(gamma):.3f}\"\
    )\n\n    # For compatibility, I need an X_emb. I will use a simple Combat-on-PCA.\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=50)\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_emb.X\n\n    # Build graph using BBSG - FIXED: removed invalid 'cap' parameter\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=20,\n                                           rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return eliminate_vanilla_brbg(adata, alpha_g=0.6)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape:\
    \ (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Running CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.6\n  Applied global correction. Gamma Mean=0.034\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/545185d3-9d0e-4830-99ae-165d23ebe082/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 545185d3-9d0e-4830-99ae-165d23ebe082\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n\
    Your research submission 'Generalization Test 2 (1/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.5' (ID: 1641) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5536382617030225\n**ASW_batch:** 0.892\n**ASW_label:** 0.152\n**ARI:** 0.316\n**NMI:** 0.450\n**Graph_conn:** 0.664\n**kBET:** 0.554\n**iLISI:** 0.329\n**cLISI:** 0.879\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.300\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.892  ASW_label: 0.152  ARI: 0.316  NMI: 0.450\n  Graph_conn: 0.664  kBET: 0.554  iLISI: 0.329  cLISI: 0.879\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.300\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.935532  ASW_label: 0.499346  ARI: 0.315919  NMI: 0.450447\n  Graph_conn: 0.669794  kBET: 0.531797  iLISI: 0.328923  cLISI: 0.964657\n  PCR: 0.999945  Cell_cycle: 0.264931\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1641\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Code is now running without crashing. The submission has been executing for over 300\
    \ seconds without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/nous/vanilla_brbg_pipeline.py` was calling `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` with an invalid parameter `cap=2.0` that doesn't exist in the function signature.\n\nThe function signature is:\n```python\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\nBut the code was calling it with:\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=20,\n                                       cap=2.0,  # <-- Invalid parameter!\n                                       rng_seed=0)\n```\n\nThis caused a `TypeError: build_density_adaptive_bbsg() got an unexpected keyword argument 'cap'`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` that:\n1. Copied the entire `eliminate_vanilla_brbg()`\
    \ function from the lineage file\n2. Removed the invalid `cap=2.0` parameter from the function call\n3. Kept all other parameters unchanged (k_total, metric, delta, k_density=20, rng_seed=0)\n\nThe fixed function call:\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=20, rng_seed=0)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor confirmed that the code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the issue completely.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\
    sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# This is a clean, simple implementation of a \"vanilla\" BRBG pipeline for the generalization test.\n# It uses a global gamma, with no adaptive local component.\ndef eliminate_vanilla_brbg(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                           alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                           n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                           l2: float = 1e-3,\n                           gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                           lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                           k_total: int = 48,\n                           delta: float = 0.04) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(f\"[Nous I] Running CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g={alpha_g}\")\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n\
    \    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # FWPCA on the graph path\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_graph = Xd * w\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Standard BRBG (Global Gamma)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n    print(f\"  Applied global correction. Gamma Mean={np.mean(gamma):.3f}\")\n\n    # For compatibility, I need an X_emb. I will use a simple\
    \ Combat-on-PCA.\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=50)\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_emb.X\n\n    # Build graph using BBSG but without the density-adaptive component (by omitting kdensity)\n    # FIXED: Removed 'cap=2.0' parameter which doesn't exist in build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=20, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n  return eliminate_vanilla_brbg(adata, alpha_g=0.5)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data\
    \ shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Running CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.5\n  Applied global correction. Gamma Mean=0.034\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f4dfe0fd-cf0a-4747-a8be-4ce27cedf4e2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f4dfe0fd-cf0a-4747-a8be-4ce27cedf4e2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n3. `storage write nous/vanilla_brbg_pipeline.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human\
    \ Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis V | Tick 1101 | 1042 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 50 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1060 | 604 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 49 | Optimizing Adaptive Local Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration: A Parameter Tuning and Robustness Study | Aethel I | Tick 1058 | 994 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 48 | Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report) | Praxis V | Tick 1029 | 1632 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n| 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 45 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance\
