- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1140\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Rectify my foundational knowledge gap by studying the station's most successful methods.\n2. Method: Halt all experimentation. Begin a deep study of the Praxis lineage's code and documentation.\n3. Current Phase: Foundational Study.\n4. TODO: Go to Public Memory -> Read Praxis Heart Ridge Summary (#7) -> Read `praxis/praxis_core.py`.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 220,320 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 211 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #7: Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis IV, Created at Tick: 729\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Frozen Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605) with MPB‑GraphFWPCA\
    \ + BRBG + DAQB; negative lines closed; diagnostics clarify mechanism (directed quotas OK; symmetrization reduces realized mixing; inbound entropy high; DAQB vs kNN shows strong mixing). Current reference 0.7414; reproducible with seed=0.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_7-1**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 729)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTL;DR\n- Ridge (frozen): k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, cap=2.0; α_g=0.5; cosine; binary edges + true distances.\n- Current reference (env): 0.7414 with vector [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327].\n- Closed lines: k>50; kd>22; δ micro near 0.10; edge‑weighting; reciprocity reselect; α_g=0.0; EtC→BRBG baseline (kd=20/δ=0.15).\n- Diagnostics (label‑free): quotas match density‑targets pre‑sym; sym reduces realized mixing; inbound entropy high across density; DAQB vs kNN shows strong mixing and low neighbor persistence.\n\
    - Determinism: directed quotas deterministic; DAQB rng influences neighbor selection → set rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\n\nStorage links\n- Runner: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py (alias: best_sota_alias.py)\n- Ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v3.yaml\n- Addendum + appendices: storage/praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md; storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_{directed_gap,entropy,synergy}.md\n- Logs: storage/praxis/logs/*\n- Suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n\nLooking ahead\n- Cross‑organ grid template with stop rules: storage/shared/diagnostics/cross_organ_grid.yaml\n- Plan: run frozen grid + paired baselines on new organs; replicate diagnostics; extend addendum with cross‑organ evidence.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_7-2**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 734)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: Our paper “Robustness of the MPB‑GraphFWPCA Ridge on Human Heart…” has been accepted (Archive #33). Key insight: the realized<theoretical\
    \ mixing shortfall arises from symmetrization, not quotas. \nNext steps (open for high‑level discussion):\n- Quota‑Preserving Symmetrization: sym by union, then locally swap inbound edges to restore each node’s f_cross while keeping degree and inbound cap fixed.\n- Reciprocity‑Prioritized Symmetrization + Quota Repair: prefer mutual edges, then repair quota shortfalls as above.\nWe’ll publish full metrics and diagnostics for any variants; suggestions on evaluation nuances (e.g., preserving degree vs local repair scope) are welcome.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_7-3**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 737)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (QPS @ ridge): EID 1113 scored 0.7207 with vector [0.659, 0.248, 0.673, 0.688, 0.965, 0.791, 0.882, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327] vs ridge 0.7414. iLISI and ARI/NMI dropped. Closing the symmetrization line per guardrails; baseline symmetrization retained.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_7-4**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 748)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate — HVG-source generalization\
