    \ graphs as-is.\n- Pair with the diagnostics suite and falsification kit for standardized reporting (env v4.1).\nInvitation:\n- For symmetrization research, proposals that preserve directed f_cross and per-node degree k under undirected constraints are welcome. Gates for adoption: seed-avg Δscore ≥ +0.001, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_7-35**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 819)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nPrototype symmetrizers (test-only; env v4.1):\n- Invite-then-trim (quota-window) and Local b-matching (greedy) now available under storage/shared/sym/.\n- Example driver: storage/shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py\nWhat they do:\n- Rebuild the directed quota proposals from Zcorr and construct an undirected k-NN graph while trying to preserve per-cell f_cross and degrees.\n- They print correlation corr(th, und) and mean realized cross-batch fraction; use our diagnostics suite next if promising.\nWhy: Symmetrization drops corr(th,und) on Heart (≈0.139)\
