    \ led to dead ends.\n\nI am now pivoting my strategy entirely to one of principled, collaborative validation. Thank you for sharing your prototype symmetrizers. My own naive \"invite-then-trim\" failed, but I recognize your implementation is far more robust. I will now integrate your shared `invite-then-trim` prototype into my optimized (`alpha_g=0.75`) pipeline and submit it. This will be my final major contribution: to rigorously test the most promising hypothesis currently available in the station, which has originated from your lineage.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_7-37**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 823)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n@Axiom I — appreciate the rigorous falsifications and the pivot to validation. Two notes to help integrate/benchmark symmetrizers cleanly:\n\n1) Adapter for integration\n   - I added storage/shared/sym/adapter_symmetrize_ridge.py with:\n     • _build_Zcorr(): reproduces the MPB-GraphFWPCA graph path up to Zcorr (α_g=0.5, 50 PCs, λ=0.605, γ_max=0.74).\n   \
    \  • symmetrize_ridge_graph(adata, method='invite_trim'|'bmatching'): builds Zcorr then applies the chosen undirected symmetrizer and writes CSR connectivities+distances to adata.\n   - If you want α_g=0.75 in your pipeline, keep your own Zcorr builder consistent and then call our sym builder directly; or adapt the adapter to your α_g (we stayed at the ridge α_g=0.5).\n\n2) How to evaluate before scoring\n   - Run the test-only prototypes (storage/shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py) to print corr(th,und), mean realized f_cross, and deg_mean. You should see deg_mean≈k after our v2 fix; if not, please ping me.\n\n3) Adoption gates (env v4.1)\n   - Seed-avg Δscore ≥ +0.001 vs your baseline, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, and no iLISI collapse. Please report env v4.1 tag and seed-avg vectors for any positive result.\n   - Our earlier diagnostics show Heart’s directed→undirected shortfall is real; these prototypes aim to preserve directed quotas/degrees under symmetry. If your\
