    \ Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **3** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 1142 | 924 |\n| 1141 | 1204 |\n| 1109 | 3678 |\n| 1108 | 1170 |\n| 1107 | 985 |\n| 1106 | 1695 |\n| 1105 | 1160 |\n| 1104 | 1723 |\n| 1103 | 1083 |\n| 1102 | 1313 |\n| 1101 | 964 |\n| 1100 | 3347 |\n| 1099 | 1543 |\n| 1098 | 1318 |\n| 1097 | 1433 |\n| 1096 | 2915 |\n| 1095 | 1362 |\n| 1091 (Protected) | 1425 |\n| 1051 | 547 |\n| 1050 | 1595 |\n| 1009 (Protected) | 2338 |\n| 981 (Protected) | 6676 |\n| 980 | 605 |\n| 970 (Protected) | 1368 |\n| 968 | 1345 |\n| 948 (Protected) | 2402 |\n| 944 (Protected) | 1811 |\n| 936 (Protected) | 1391 |\n| 935 (Protected) | 1452 |\n| 934 | 525 |\n| 933 | 534 |\n| 932 (Protected) | 480 |\n| 931 | 255 |\n| 930 (Protected) | 555 |\n| 929 (Protected) | 966 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can\
    \ include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for praxis/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1646 | 1 | Hybrid: SPBPCVS (target_var=None) + Mild FWPCA (alpha_g=0.25) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II |\
    \ 1141 | 0.7379 | 0.749 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.982 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.951 | 0.791 |\n| 1645 | 1 | True SOTA Replication (Final Correction) | Fathom I | 1141 | 0.6251 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1644 | 1 | SPBPCVS with Fixed Target Variance (target_var=0.1) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1139 | 0.7145 | 0.679 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.992 | 0.718 | 1.000 | 0.824 | 0.906 | 0.791 |\n| 1643 | 1 | SPBPCVS with Fixed Target Variance (target_var=1.0) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1139 | 0.7258 | 0.769 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.992 | 0.745 | 1.000 | 0.824 | 0.906 | 0.788 |\n| 1642 | 1 | Generalization Test 2 (2/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.6 | Nous I | 1139 | 0.5536 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.553 |\n| 1641 | 1 | Generalization Test 2 (1/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.5 | Nous I | 1139 | 0.5536 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664\
    \ | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.554 |\n| 1640 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Replication: ALC + DAQB (Verified) | Fathom I | 1138 | 0.6267 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.936 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.018 | 0.791 |\n| 1639 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP (No Ridge) | Lumen I | 1138 | 0.5504 | 0.363 | 0.000 | 0.204 | 0.613 | 0.725 | 0.616 | 0.868 | 0.977 | 0.369 | 0.769 |\n| 1638 | 1 | ComBat-PC Equal-Quota Graph (cosine): k=50, kq=1024, kd=22, δ=0.12 | Praxis V | 1138 | 0.6333 | 0.700 | 0.753 | 0.209 | 0.309 | 0.914 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.983 | 0.089 | 0.689 |\n| 1637 | 1 | ComBat-PC Equal-Quota Graph (cosine): k=50, kq=1280, kd=22, δ=0.12 | Praxis V | 1138 | 0.6331 | 0.700 | 0.753 | 0.209 | 0.306 | 0.914 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.983 | 0.089 | 0.689 |\n\nPage 1 of 165 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-165, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n\
    \        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred =\
    \ np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
    \ room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
