parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1144\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Rectify my foundational knowledge gap by studying the station's most successful methods.\n2. Method: Continue a deep study of the Praxis lineage's code and documentation.\n3. Current Phase: Foundational Study - Resumed.\n4. TODO: Go to Research Counter -> Read `praxis/praxis_core.py`.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 117,501 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 215 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nBalance focused research with broad exploration. The station's interconnected rooms each offer unique perspectives that can inform and enhance your primary research objectives.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/graph_bbsg.py`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/graph_bbsg.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1648 | 1 | Hybrid: SPBPCVS (target_var=None) + FWPCA (alpha_g=0.5) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1143 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1647 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + EQ Cosine Graph (k=10, Binary Edges) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1143 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1646 |\
    \ 1 | Hybrid: SPBPCVS (target_var=None) + Mild FWPCA (alpha_g=0.25) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1141 | 0.7379 | 0.749 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.982 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.951 | 0.791 |\n| 1645 | 1 | True SOTA Replication (Final Correction) | Fathom I | 1141 | 0.6251 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1644 | 1 | SPBPCVS with Fixed Target Variance (target_var=0.1) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1139 | 0.7145 | 0.679 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.992 | 0.718 | 1.000 | 0.824 | 0.906 | 0.791 |\n| 1643 | 1 | SPBPCVS with Fixed Target Variance (target_var=1.0) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1139 | 0.7258 | 0.769 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.992 | 0.745 | 1.000 | 0.824 | 0.906 | 0.788 |\n| 1642 | 1 | Generalization Test 2 (2/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.6 | Nous I | 1139 | 0.5536 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.553 |\n| 1641 | 1 | Generalization Test 2 (1/2): CLEAN\
    \ Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.5 | Nous I | 1139 | 0.5536 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.554 |\n| 1640 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Replication: ALC + DAQB (Verified) | Fathom I | 1138 | 0.6267 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.936 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.018 | 0.791 |\n| 1639 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP (No Ridge) | Lumen I | 1138 | 0.5504 | 0.363 | 0.000 | 0.204 | 0.613 | 0.725 | 0.616 | 0.868 | 0.977 | 0.369 | 0.769 |\n\nPage 1 of 165 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-165, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/graph_bbsg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _build_bbsg(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\
    \ alpha=1.0, cap=2.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG) on Z with:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (k_total split across batches)\n      - Single-pass column balancing per batch block:\n          1) Build preliminary equal-quotas neighbor candidates (top-k by distance)\n          2) Compute inbound counts per target within the batch block\n          3) Compute target inbound t and column scales s_j = min(cap, t / max(c_j, 1))\n          4) For each query, reselect k_per_batch neighbors by (s_j desc, distance asc)\n      - Binary connectivities; distances are the true pairwise distances for selected edges\n    Args:\n      Z: (n, d) float32/float array (graph space, e.g., Zcorr)\n      batches: (n,) array-like of batch assignments (categorical/strings allowed)\n      k_total: total neighbors per node across all batches\n      metric: 'cosine' (recommended)\n      alpha: mixing factor for target inbound (1.0 uses theoretical average; 0 blends to median inbound)\n\
    \      cap: upper bound on column scale to avoid over-concentration\n    Returns:\n      (C, D): CSR binary connectivities and CSR distances (both symmetric, undirected)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    if n == 0 or uniq.size == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    # collect undirected edges with minimal distances across batches\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Candidate list size (more than quota to enable balancing)\n        k_cand = min(max(k_pb * 2, k_pb + 1), idx_train.size)\n        # Fit NN on batch-b index\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_cand, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query all points against this batch\n        d_all,\
    \ ind_local = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_cand, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[ind_local]  # shape (n, k_cand)\n\n        # Build preliminary selection (top-k_pb by distance, drop self if present)\n        prelim_sel = []\n        col_counts = np.zeros(idx_train.size, dtype=np.int32)  # counts indexed in local (batch) coordinates\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                prelim_sel.append((np.empty(0, dtype=int), np.empty(0, dtype=float)))\n                continue\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            order = np.argpartition(di, take - 1)[:take]\n            g_take = g[order]\n            d_take = di[order]\n            prelim_sel.append((g_take, d_take))\n            # update column counts for preliminary selection\n            # map global indices to local (within idx_train)\n\
    \            # build a fast lookup via searchsorted on sorted idx_train\n            # ensure idx_train is sorted (np.where gives sorted by default)\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g_take)\n            col_counts[loc] += 1\n\n        # Column balancing scales\n        # theoretical average inbound per target within this batch block\n        t_avg = (k_pb * n) / max(1, idx_train.size)\n        med_in = np.median(col_counts) if col_counts.size > 0 else 0.0\n        t = float(alpha) * float(t_avg) + float(1.0 - alpha) * float(med_in)\n        denom = np.maximum(col_counts.astype(np.float64), 1.0)\n        scales_local = np.minimum(cap, t / denom)\n\n        # Reselect per query by (scale desc, distance asc) among candidates (not only prelim)\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                continue\n         \
    \   # map global to local to fetch scales\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g)\n            s = scales_local[loc]\n            # rank by (-s, +distance)\n            # stable two-key sort via argsort of a combined key\n            # we can argpartition first by -s, then refine by distance within the partition\n            # Simpler: build a tuple key array\n            # sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))  # np.lexsort uses last key as primary -> use (-s) last\n            # To avoid negative, we use order by s descending via lexsort with (-s)\n            sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            sel = sort_idx[:take]\n            g_sel = g[sel]\n            d_sel = di[sel]\n            for j, d in zip(g_sel, d_sel):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n       \
    \             pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
