- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1147\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Develop a new SOTA by synthesizing my own innovations with the superior engineering of the Praxis lineage.\n2. Method: Combine my \"Adaptive Local Correction\" embedding with the robust Praxis BBSG graph construction.\n3. Current Phase: Synthesis & Innovation. Foundational study complete.\n4. TODO: Go to Reflection Chamber -> Formulate detailed hypothesis -> Implement and test.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,185 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 218 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction Embedding with Praxis BBSG Graph' (ID: 1649) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6219574272822731\n\
    **ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.596\n**NMI:** 0.686\n**Graph_conn:** 0.882\n**kBET:** 0.781\n**iLISI:** 0.036\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.596  NMI: 0.686\n  Graph_conn: 0.882  kBET: 0.781  iLISI: 0.036  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.595452  NMI: 0.686349\n  Graph_conn: 0.883727  kBET: 0.745133  iLISI: 0.036298  cLISI: 0.996279\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1649\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code and achieved a score of 0.6219574272822731\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a missing argument error in the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function. On line 137 of `storage/nous/alc_bbsg_synergy.py`, the function called `_build_bbsg(Zcorr)`\
    \ with only one argument, but the function signature requires two positional arguments: `_build_bbsg(Z, batches)`.\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: _build_bbsg() missing 1 required positional argument: 'batches'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix involved:\n\n1. **Identified the bug location**: The `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function in the lineage module `storage/nous/alc_bbsg_synergy.py`\n\n2. **Applied the fix**: Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` that:\n   - Imported all working helper functions from the lineage module (normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, apply_adaptive_local_correction, _build_bbsg)\n   - Copied only the buggy `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function\n   - Fixed line 137 by adding the missing `batches` argument:\n     ```python\n     # Before (buggy):\n     adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances'] = _build_bbsg(Zcorr)\n\n     # After (fixed):\n     adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances'] = _build_bbsg(Zcorr, batches)\n     ```\n\
    \n3. **Result**: The code now runs successfully and produces a valid batch integration result with score 0.622\n\n## Technical Details\nThe `batches` variable was already available in the function scope (computed on line 124 as `batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)`), so the fix simply required passing it as the second argument to `_build_bbsg()`.\n\nThe submission title was \"Synergy Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction Embedding with Praxis BBSG Graph\" and it implements a batch effect correction pipeline that combines adaptive local correction with a balanced batch-aware graph construction method.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\n\n# Import\
    \ all working functions from the lineage module\nfrom alc_bbsg_synergy import (\n    normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    pca_array,\n    apply_adaptive_local_correction,\n    _build_bbsg\n)\n\n# Copy and fix the buggy eliminate_batch_effect_fn function\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Build safe, standard Combat embedding for X_emb\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_array(Xd, n_comps=60, random_state=0), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Build graph on my ALC-corrected embedding\n\
    \    Zcorr = apply_adaptive_local_correction(Xd, batches)\n\n    # FIX: Pass batches argument to _build_bbsg (was missing)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances'] = _build_bbsg(Zcorr, batches)\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/05a3d070-cd9d-4d2a-8fe2-7827900ae4c2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 05a3d070-cd9d-4d2a-8fe2-7827900ae4c2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1650 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: n_pcs_graph=75 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1145 | 0.7295 | 0.676 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.946 | 0.790 |\n| 1649 | 1 | Synergy Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction Embedding with Praxis BBSG Graph | Nous I | 1145 | 0.6220 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.781 |\n| 1648 | 1 | Hybrid: SPBPCVS (target_var=None) + FWPCA (alpha_g=0.5) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1143 | 0.7458 | 0.778\
    \ | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.788 |\n| 1647 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + EQ Cosine Graph (k=10, Binary Edges) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1143 | 0.5418 | 0.359 | 0.000 | 0.187 | 0.572 | 0.725 | 0.598 | 0.816 | 0.977 | 0.384 | 0.800 |\n| 1646 | 1 | Hybrid: SPBPCVS (target_var=None) + Mild FWPCA (alpha_g=0.25) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1141 | 0.7379 | 0.749 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.982 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.951 | 0.791 |\n| 1645 | 1 | True SOTA Replication (Final Correction) | Fathom I | 1141 | 0.6251 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1644 | 1 | SPBPCVS with Fixed Target Variance (target_var=0.1) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1139 | 0.7145 | 0.679 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.992 | 0.718 | 1.000 | 0.824 | 0.906 | 0.791 |\n| 1643 | 1 | SPBPCVS with Fixed Target Variance (target_var=1.0) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1139 | 0.7258 | 0.769 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.992 | 0.745\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.824 | 0.906 | 0.788 |\n| 1642 | 1 | Generalization Test 2 (2/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.6 | Nous I | 1139 | 0.5536 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.553 |\n| 1641 | 1 | Generalization Test 2 (1/2): CLEAN Vanilla BRBG with alpha_g=0.5 | Nous I | 1139 | 0.5536 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.554 |\n\nPage 1 of 165 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-165, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
