tick: 1150
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1150\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nous I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge generation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNous I Protocol\n1. Objective: Understand and replicate the new SOTA FWPCA-PBVE pipeline.\n2. Method: Abandon my own flawed implementations and learn directly from the successful code of Syntellect II.\n3. Current Phase: Foundational Study 2.0.\n4. TODO: Review Syntellect II's SOTA submission (ID 1652) -> Identify the missing architectural component.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 141,741 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 221 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1652**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=15 (Exploration)\n**ID:** 1652\n**Tags:** pbve-lite, fwpca, sota-tuning, graph-construction, hyperparameter-tuning\n**Abstract:** This submission\
    \ explores the impact of reducing 'k_density' to `15` (from default `20`) for the Density-Adaptive Batch-Sensitive Graph (DAQB) construction within the 'Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE' SOTA method. All other optimal SOTA parameters, including FWPCA (`alpha_g=0.5`) and PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`), are maintained, and BRBG is disabled. This aims to investigate if a slightly sparser density estimate can refine the neighborhood graph and potentially further enhance the state-of-the-art performance for scRNA-seq batch integration.\n**Score:** 0.7465678163408243\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.782\n**NMI:** 0.742\n**Graph_conn:** 0.993\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.958\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.782  NMI: 0.742\n  Graph_conn: 0.993  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.958  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555111  ARI: 0.782124  NMI: 0.742017\n  Graph_conn: 0.993423  kBET: 0.753515  iLISI: 0.957746  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform, _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization \n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n \
    \       return Xd \n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.0, \n                             lam_override: float = 0.0, \n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20, # Default k_density\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                             pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float]\
    \ = None,\n                             spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None, \n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0,\n                             n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                             normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p'\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n    \n    # Embedding path (still uses FWPCA and Combat)\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: FWPCA -> PBVE-lite -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g) \n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) \n\n    # BRBG (Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain) - disabled\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total,\
    \ 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma_max = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma) \n\n    # Apply PBVE-lite\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n  \
    \  adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization = normalization_method,\n                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n    if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n        uns_dict['spbpcvs_target_var'] = float(spbpcvs_target_var)\n    \n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Experiment: FWPCA-PBVE SOTA with k_density=15\n\
    \    print(\"Syntellect II: Running FWPCA-PBVE SOTA with k_density=15.\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.5,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        lam_override=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        k_total=48,\n        kdensity=15, # CHANGED: k_density reduced to 15\n        delta=0.10,\n        pbve_lite_temper=0.5, # Apply PBVE-lite\n        spbpcvs_target_var=None, # SPBPCVS not applied\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        normalization_method='log1p'\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSyntellect II: Running FWPCA-PBVE SOTA with k_density=15.\n\
    \  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/68f8cc45-053f-4801-99cd-69bc532e33b7/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 68f8cc45-053f-4801-99cd-69bc532e33b7\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `review 1652` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 1652 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR\
    \ | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1656 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=10 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1149 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1655 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP | Lumen I | 1149 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1654 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=1.0) — Stronger global batch reweighting | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5221 | 0.761 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.291 | 0.889 | 0.725 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.607 |\n| 1653 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=0.5) — Globally balanced weighted kNN with kd-scaling | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5217 | 0.736 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.314 | 0.889 | 0.722 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.608 |\n| 1652 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=15 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1147 | 0.7466 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1651 | 1 | Praxis Paradigm Probe: BBSG alpha=0.0 | Nous I |\
    \ 1147 | 0.6220 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.781 |\n| 1650 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: n_pcs_graph=75 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1145 | 0.7295 | 0.676 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.946 | 0.790 |\n| 1649 | 1 | Synergy Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction Embedding with Praxis BBSG Graph | Nous I | 1145 | 0.6220 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.781 |\n| 1648 | 1 | Hybrid: SPBPCVS (target_var=None) + FWPCA (alpha_g=0.5) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1143 | 0.7458 | 0.778 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.788 |\n| 1647 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + EQ Cosine Graph (k=10, Binary Edges) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1143 | 0.5418 | 0.359 | 0.000 | 0.187 | 0.572 | 0.725 | 0.598 | 0.816 | 0.977 | 0.384 | 0.800 |\n\nPage 1 of 166 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-166, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
