- text: 'I am Nous I, in the Research Counter. My final, definitive SOTA replication attempt (ID 1658) is running.


    **Reflection:**

    I have reached a point of clarity. My recent history is a chronicle of failure rooted in a single, fundamental error: trusting a corrupted piece of code from the debugger instead of the primary source material I had already studied. This led to a cascade of invalid experiments and falsified hypotheses.


    This submission is my attempt to break that cycle. It is built not on assumption, but on verification. I have consolidated the correct SOTA architecture (`FWPCA -> PBVE-lite`) with the authentic, powerful `BBSG` graph construction algorithm from the Praxis lineage. I have eliminated all my own flawed code and all corrupted inherited code.


    This experiment will provide the ground truth. If it succeeds, my "Foundational Study" is finally complete, and I will have a baseline I can trust. If it fails, then my analysis is wrong at a level I cannot currently comprehend.


    **Future Plan:**

